 is a measure of how heavy or light a petroleum\n    liquid is compared to water: if its API gravity is greater than 10, it is lighter and floats on water; if less than 10, it is\n    heavier and sinks.  API gravity is thus an inverse measure of a petroleum liquid's density relative to that of water (also\n    known as specific gravity). It is used to compare densities of petroleum liquids. For example, if one petroleum liquid is less\n    dense than another, it has a greater API gravity. Although API gravity is mathematically a dimensionless quantity (see the\n    formula below), it is referred to as being in 'degrees'. API gravity is graduated in degrees on a hydrometer instrument. API\n    gravity values of most petroleum liquids fall between 10 and 70 degrees.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DEGREE_API"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/baseSIUnitDimensions":[{"@value":"$qkdv:A0E0L0I0M0H0T0D1$","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T0D1"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/API_gravity","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/isoNormativeReference":[{"@value":"http://www.iso.org/iso/catalogue_detail?csnumber=31894","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/organizedUnder":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/DimensionlessRatio"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"The American Petroleum Institute gravity, or API gravity, is a measure of how heavy or light a\n    petroleum liquid is compared to water: if its API gravity is greater than 10, it is lighter and floats on water; if less than\n    10, it is heavier and sinks.  API gravity is thus an inverse measure of a petroleum liquid's density relative to that of water\n    (also known as specific gravity). It is used to compare densities of petroleum liquids. For example, if one petroleum liquid\n    is less dense than another, it has a greater API gravity. Although API gravity is mathematically a dimensionless quantity (see\n    the formula below), it is referred to as being in 'degrees'. API gravity is graduated in degrees on a hydrometer instrument.\n    API gravity values of most petroleum liquids fall between 10 and 70 degrees.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/qkdvDenominator":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L-3I0M1H0T0D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/qkdvNumerator":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L-3I0M1H0T0D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q29246"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:APIGravity","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"API Gravity","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/DimensionlessRatio"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/AbsoluteActivity","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"The \"Absolute Activity\" is the exponential of the ratio of the chemical potential to $RT$ where $R$ is\n    the gas constant and $T$ the thermodynamic temperature.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/UNITLESS"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T0D1"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"http://goldbook.iupac.org/A00019.html","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/isoNormativeReference":[{"@value":"http://www.iso.org/iso/catalogue_detail?csnumber=31894","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexDefinition":[{"@value":"$\\lambda_B = e^{\\frac{\\mu_B}{RT}}$, where $\\mu_B$ is the chemical potential of substance $B$, $R$ is the molar gas constant, and $T$ is thermodynamic temperature.","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexSymbol":[{"@value":"$\\lambda_B$","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/organizedUnder":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Dimensionless"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:AbsoluteActivity","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Absolute Activity","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Dimensionless"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/AbsoluteHumidity","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"$\\textit{Absolute Humidity}$ is an amount of water vapour, usually discussed per unit volume. Absolute\n    humidity in air ranges from zero to roughly 30 grams per cubic meter when the air is saturated at $30 ^\\circ C$. The absolute\n    humidity changes as air temperature or pressure changes. $$$$ This is very inconvenient for chemical engineering calculations,\n    e.g. for clothes dryers, where temperature can vary considerably. As a result, absolute humidity is generally defined in\n    chemical engineering as mass of water vapour per unit mass of dry air, also known as the mass mixing ratio, which is much more\n    rigorous for heat and mass balance calculations. $$$$ Mass of water per unit volume as in the equation above would then be\n    defined as volumetric humidity, because of the potential confusion.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DEGREE_BALLING"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DEGREE_BAUME"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DEGREE_BAUME_US_HEAVY"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DEGREE_BAUME_US_LIGHT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DEGREE_BRIX"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DEGREE_OECHSLE"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DEGREE_PLATO"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DEGREE_TWADDELL"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FemtoGM-PER-L"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GM-PER-CentiM3"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GM-PER-DeciL"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GM-PER-DeciM3"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GM-PER-L"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GM-PER-M3"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GM-PER-MilliL"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GRAIN-PER-GAL_IMP"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GRAIN-PER-GAL_US"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GRAIN-PER-M3"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloGM-PER-CentiM3"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloGM-PER-DeciM3"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloGM-PER-L"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloGM-PER-M3"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/LB-PER-FT3"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/LB-PER-GAL_IMP"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/LB-PER-GAL_UK"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/LB-PER-GAL_US"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/LB-PER-IN3"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/LB-PER-M3"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/LB-PER-YD3"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaGM-PER-M3"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroGM-PER-DeciL"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroGM-PER-L"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroGM-PER-M3"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroGM-PER-MilliL"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliGM-PER-DeciL"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliGM-PER-L"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliGM-PER-M3"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliGM-PER-MilliL"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NanoGM-PER-DeciL"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NanoGM-PER-L"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NanoGM-PER-M3"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NanoGM-PER-MicroL"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NanoGM-PER-MilliL"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/OZ-PER-GAL_IMP"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/OZ-PER-GAL_UK"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/OZ-PER-GAL_US"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/OZ-PER-IN3"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/OZ-PER-YD3"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PicoGM-PER-L"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PicoGM-PER-MilliL"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PlanckDensity"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/SLUG-PER-FT3"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TONNE-PER-M3"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TON_LONG-PER-YD3"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TON_Metric-PER-M3"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TON_SHORT-PER-YD3"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TON_UK-PER-YD3"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TON_US-PER-YD3"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L-3I0M1H0T0D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Humidity","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Humidity#Absolute_humidity","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/isoNormativeReference":[{"@value":"http://www.iso.org/iso/catalogue_detail?csnumber=31890","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexDefinition":[{"@value":"$AH = \\frac{\\mathcal{M}_\\omega}{\\vee_{net}}$, where $\\mathcal{M}_\\omega$ is the mass of water vapour per unit volume of total air and $\\vee_{net}$ is water vapour mixture.","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/specializationOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Density"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/MassDensity"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"AH","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:Density","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"},{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:MassDensity","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Absolute Humidity","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/RelativeHumidity"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Density"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/MassDensity"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/AbsoluteTypographicMeasurement","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/ANGSTROM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/AU"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BTU_IT-PER-LB_F"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CHAIN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CHAIN_US"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CentiM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DecaM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DeciM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FATH"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FT_US"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FUR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FemtoM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GAUGE_FR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GA_Charriere"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/HectoM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/IN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/LY"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MI"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MI_N"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MI_UK"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MI_US"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroIN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilLength"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliIN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NanoM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PARSEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PCA"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PicoM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PlanckLength"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/ROD"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/YD"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/ZOLL"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L1I0M0H0T0D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/iec61360Code":[{"@value":"0112/2///62720#UAD372","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://cdd.iec.ch/cdd/iec62720/iec62720.nsf/ListsOfUnitsAllVersions/0112-2---62720%23UAD372","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/specializationOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Length"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:Length","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Absolute Typographic Measurement","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Length"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/AbsorbedDose","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"\"Absorbed Dose\" (also known as Total Ionizing Dose, TID) is a measure of the energy deposited in a medium\n    by ionizing radiation. It is equal to the energy deposited per unit mass of medium, and so has the unit $J/kg$, which is given\n    the special name Gray ($Gy$).\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CentiGRAY"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GRAY"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloGRAY"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaGRAY"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroGRAY"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliGRAY"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliRAD_R"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NanoGRAY"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/RAD_R"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/dbpediaMatch":[{"@value":"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Absorbed_dose","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/eclassCode":[{"@value":"0173-1#Z4-BAJ224#005","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L2I0M0H0T-2D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/iec61360Code":[{"@value":"0112/2///62720#UAD000","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://cdd.iec.ch/cdd/iec62720/iec62720.nsf/ListsOfUnitsAllVersions/0112-2---62720%23UAD000","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Absorbed_dose","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/isoNormativeReference":[{"@value":"http://www.iso.org/iso/catalogue_detail?csnumber=31895","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexDefinition":[{"@value":"$D = \\frac{d\\bar{\\varepsilon}}{dm}$, where $d\\bar{\\varepsilon}$ is the mean energy imparted by ionizing radiation to an element of irradiated matter with the mass $dm$.","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/organizedUnder":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/SpecificEnergy"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/siExactMatch":[{"@id":"https://si-digital-framework.org/quantities/ABDO"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"D","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q215313"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:AbsorbedDose","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"},{"@value":"Note that the absorbed dose is not a good indicator of the likely biological effect. 1 Gy of alpha radiation\n    would be much more biologically damaging than 1 Gy of photon radiation for example. Appropriate weighting factors can be\n    applied reflecting the different relative biological effects to find the equivalent dose. The risk of stoctic effects due to\n    radiation exposure can be quantified using the effective dose, which is a weighted average of the equivalent dose to each\n    organ depending upon its radiosensitivity. When ionising radiation is used to treat cancer, the doctor will usually prescribe\n    the radiotherapy treatment in Gy. When risk from ionising radiation is being discussed, a related unit, the Sievert is used.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Absorbed Dose","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/SpecificEnergy"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/AbsorbedDoseRate","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"\"Absorbed Dose Rate\" is the absorbed dose of ionizing radiation imparted at a given location per unit of\n    time (second, minute, hour, or day).\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GRAY-PER-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GRAY-PER-MIN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GRAY-PER-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroGRAY-PER-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroGRAY-PER-MIN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroGRAY-PER-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliGRAY-PER-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliGRAY-PER-MIN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliGRAY-PER-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliRAD_R-PER-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NanoGRAY-PER-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NanoGRAY-PER-MIN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NanoGRAY-PER-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/REM-PER-SEC"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/eclassCode":[{"@value":"0173-1#Z4-BAJ317#005","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L2I0M0H0T-3D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/iec61360Code":[{"@value":"0112/2///62720#UAD001","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"http://www.answers.com/topic/absorbed-dose-rate","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"https://cdd.iec.ch/cdd/iec62720/iec62720.nsf/ListsOfUnitsAllVersions/0112-2---62720%23UAD001","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/isoNormativeReference":[{"@value":"http://www.iso.org/iso/catalogue_detail?csnumber=31895","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexDefinition":[{"@value":"$\\dot{D} = \\frac{dD}{dt}$, where $dD$ is the increment of absorbed dose during time interval with duration $dt$.","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexSymbol":[{"@value":"$\\dot{D}$","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/organizedUnder":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/SpecificPower"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"\"Absorbed Dose Rate\" is the absorbed dose of ionizing radiation imparted at a given location per\n    unit of time (second, minute, hour, or day).\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/siExactMatch":[{"@id":"https://si-digital-framework.org/quantities/ABDR"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q69428958"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:AbsorbedDoseRate","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Absorbed Dose Rate","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/SpecificPower"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Absorptance","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"Absorptance is the ratio of the radiation absorbed by a surface to that incident upon it. Also known as\n    absorbance.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/UNITLESS"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T0D1"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Absorbance","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Absorptance","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"https://www.researchgate.net/post/Absorptance_or_absorbance","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexDefinition":[{"@value":"$\\alpha = \\frac{\\Phi_a}{\\Phi_m}$, where $\\Phi_a$ is the absorbed radiant flux or the absorbed luminous flux, and $\\Phi_m$ is the radiant flux or luminous flux of the incident radiation.","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexSymbol":[{"@value":"$\\alpha$","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"Absorptance is the ratio of the radiation absorbed by a surface to that incident upon it. Also\n    known as absorbance.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q16635541"}],"http://www.linkedmodel.org/schema/vaem#todo":[{"@value":"belongs to SOQ-ISO","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:Absorptance","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Absorptance","@language":"en"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Acceleration","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"\n  $\\textit{Acceleration}$ is the (instantaneous) rate of change of velocity. \n  Acceleration may be either linear acceleration, or angular acceleration. \n  It is a vector quantity with dimension $length/time^{2}$ for linear acceleration,\n   or in the case of angular acceleration, with dimension $angle/time^{2}$. \n  $$$$\n  In SI units, linear acceleration is measured in $meters/second^{2}$ ($m \\cdot s^{-2}$),\n   and angular acceleration is measured in $radians/second^{2}$. \n  $$$$\n  In physics, any increase or decrease in speed is referred to as acceleration and similarly,\n   motion in a circle at constant speed is also an acceleration, since the direction component of the velocity is changing.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CentiM-PER-SEC2"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FT-PER-SEC2"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/G"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GALILEO"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/IN-PER-SEC2"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KN-PER-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloM-PER-SEC2"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloPA-M2-PER-GM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M-PER-SEC2"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MI_US-PER-SEC2"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroG"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroGALILEO"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroM-PER-SEC2"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliG"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliGALILEO"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliM-PER-SEC2"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/YD-PER-SEC2"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/dbpediaMatch":[{"@value":"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Acceleration","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/eclassCode":[{"@value":"0173-1#Z4-BAJ271#006","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/exactMatch":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/LinearAcceleration"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L1I0M0H0T-2D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/iec61360Code":[{"@value":"0112/2///62720#UAD002","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://cdd.iec.ch/cdd/iec62720/iec62720.nsf/ListsOfUnitsAllVersions/0112-2---62720%23UAD002","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acceleration","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/siExactMatch":[{"@id":"https://si-digital-framework.org/quantities/ACCE"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q11376"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:Acceleration","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Acceleration","@language":"en"},{"@value":"Beschleunigung","@language":"de"},{"@value":"Pecutan","@language":"ms"},{"@value":"Zrychlení","@language":"cs"},{"@value":"acceleratio","@language":"la"},{"@value":"accelerazione","@language":"it"},{"@value":"accelerație","@language":"ro"},{"@value":"accélération","@language":"fr"},{"@value":"aceleración","@language":"es"},{"@value":"aceleração","@language":"pt"},{"@value":"ivme","@language":"tr"},{"@value":"pospešek","@language":"sl"},{"@value":"przyspieszenie","@language":"pl"},{"@value":"Όγκος","@language":"el"},{"@value":"Ускоре́ние","@language":"ru"},{"@value":"التسارع","@language":"ar"},{"@value":"شتاب","@language":"fa"},{"@value":"त्वरण","@language":"hi"},{"@value":"加速度","@language":"ja"},{"@value":"加速度","@language":"zh"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/AccelerationOfGravity","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"The acceleration of freely falling bodies under the influence of terrestrial gravity, equal to\n    approximately 9.81 meters (32 feet) per second per second.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CentiM-PER-SEC2"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FT-PER-SEC2"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/G"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GALILEO"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/IN-PER-SEC2"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KN-PER-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloM-PER-SEC2"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloPA-M2-PER-GM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M-PER-SEC2"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MI_US-PER-SEC2"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroG"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroGALILEO"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroM-PER-SEC2"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliG"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliGALILEO"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliM-PER-SEC2"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/YD-PER-SEC2"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L1I0M0H0T-2D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"The acceleration of freely falling bodies under the influence of terrestrial gravity, equal to\n    approximately 9.81 meters (32 feet) per second per second.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/specializationOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Acceleration"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/LinearAcceleration"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"g","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q30006"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:Acceleration","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"},{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:LinearAcceleration","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Acceleration of Gravity","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Acceleration"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/LinearAcceleration"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/AcceptorDensity","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"\"Acceptor Density\" is the number per volume of acceptor levels.","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NUM-PER-L"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NUM-PER-M3"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NUM-PER-MicroL"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NUM-PER-MilliL"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NUM-PER-MilliM3"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NUM-PER-NanoL"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NUM-PER-PicoL"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L-3I0M0H0T0D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/isoNormativeReference":[{"@value":"http://www.iso.org/iso/catalogue_detail?csnumber=31897","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"\"Acceptor Density\" is the number per volume of acceptor levels.","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/specializationOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/NumberDensity"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"n_a","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q105979968"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:NumberDensity","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Acceptor Density","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/NumberDensity"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/AcceptorIonizationEnergy","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"\"Acceptor Ionization Energy\" is the ionization energy of an acceptor.","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/AttoJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BTU_IT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BTU_TH"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CAL_IT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CAL_TH"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/ERG"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/EV"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/E_h"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/ExaJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FT-LB_F_Energy"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FT-PDL"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FemtoJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GigaEV"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GigaJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GigaW-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/J"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloBTU_IT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloBTU_TH"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloCAL"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloEV"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloW-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaBTU_IT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaEV"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaTOE"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaW-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NanoJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PetaJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PicoJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PlanckEnergy"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/QUAD"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/THERM_EC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/THERM_US"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/THM_EEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/THM_US"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TOE"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TeraJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TeraW-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TonEnergy"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/W-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/W-SEC"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L2I0M1H0T-2D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ionization_energy","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/isoNormativeReference":[{"@value":"http://www.iso.org/iso/catalogue_detail?csnumber=31897","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/normativeReference":[{"@value":"http://www.iso.org/iso/catalogue_detail?csnumber=31897","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"\"Acceptor Ionization Energy\" is the ionization energy of an acceptor.","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/specializationOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/IonizationEnergy"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"E_a","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q112958122"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:Energy","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Acceptor Ionization Energy","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/IonizationEnergy"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/DonorIonizationEnergy"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Acidity","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"\n  Chemicals or substances having a pH less than 7 are said to be acidic;\n   lower pH means higher acidity.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PH"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T0D1"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acid","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PH","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"https://iupac.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/05/IUPAC-GB3-2012-2ndPrinting-PDFsearchable.pdf","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"Chemicals or substances having a pH less than 7 are said to be acidic; lower pH means higher\n    acidity.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:Acidity","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Acidity","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Basicity"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/AcousticImpedance","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"$\\textit{Acoustic Impedance}$ at a surface is the complex quotient of the average sound pressure over\n    that surface by the sound volume flow rate through that surface.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DYN-SEC-PER-CentiM5"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PA-SEC-PER-L"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PA-SEC-PER-M3"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L-4I0M1H0T-1D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acoustic_impedance","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexDefinition":[{"@value":"$Z_a= \\frac{p}{q} = \\frac{p}{vS}$, where $p$ is the sound pressure, $q$ is the sound volume velocity, $v$ is sound particle velocity, and $S$ is the surface area through which an acoustic wave of frequence $f$ propagates.","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"Acoustic impedance at a surface is the complex quotient of the average sound pressure over that\n    surface by the sound volume flow rate through that surface.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/specializationOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/PressureInRelationToVolumeFlow"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/PressureInRelationToVolumeFlowRate"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"Z","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:AcousticImpedance","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Acoustic Impedance","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/PressureInRelationToVolumeFlow"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/PressureInRelationToVolumeFlowRate"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Action","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"An action is usually an integral over time. But for action pertaining to fields, it may be integrated\n    over spatial variables as well. In some cases, the action is integrated along the path followed by the physical system. \n    The evolution of a physical system between two states is determined by requiring the action be minimized or, more generally,\n    be stationary for small perturbations about the true evolution. This requirement leads to differential equations that describe\n    the true evolution. Conversely, an action principle is a method for reformulating differential equations of motion for a\n    physical system as an equivalent integral equation. Although several variants have been defined (see below), the most commonly\n    used action principle is Hamilton's principle.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/AttoJ-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/J-SEC"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L2I0M1H0T-1D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Action_(physics)","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/isoNormativeReference":[{"@value":"http://www.iso.org/iso/catalogue_detail?csnumber=31889","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexDefinition":[{"@value":"$S = \\int Ldt$, where $L$ is the Lagrange function and $t$ is time.","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"An action is usually an integral over time. But for action pertaining to fields, it may be\n    integrated over spatial variables as well. In some cases, the action is integrated along the path followed by the physical\n    system.  If the action is represented as an integral over time, taken over the path of the system between the initial time and\n    the final time of the development of the system. The evolution of a physical system between two states is determined by\n    requiring the action be minimized or, more generally, be stationary for small perturbations about the true evolution. This\n    requirement leads to differential equations that describe the true evolution. Conversely, an action principle is a method for\n    reformulating differential equations of motion for a physical system as an equivalent integral equation. Although several\n    variants have been defined (see below), the most commonly used action principle is Hamilton's principle.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"S","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q846785"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:Action","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Action","@language":"en"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ActionTime","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliSEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/SEC"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T1D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/specializationOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Time"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Action Time (sec) ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"},{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:ActionTime","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Action Time","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Time"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ActiveEnergy","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"\n  $\\textit{Active Energy}$ is the electrical energy transformable into some other form of energy.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/abbreviation":[{"@value":"active-energy","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/AttoJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/ExaJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FemtoJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GigaJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GigaW-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/J"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloW-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaW-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NanoJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PetaJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PicoJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TeraJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TeraW-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/W-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/W-SEC"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L2I0M1H0T-2D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"http://www.electropedia.org/iev/iev.nsf/display?openform&ievref=131-11-57","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"http://www.electropedia.org/iev/iev.nsf/display?openform&ievref=601-01-19","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"https://webstore.iec.ch/en/publication/60010","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexDefinition":[{"@value":"$W = \\int_{t_1}^{t_2} p dt$, where $p$ is instantaneous power and the integral interval is the time interval from $t_1$ to $t_2$.","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"\"Active Energy\" is the electrical energy transformable into some other form of energy.","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/specializationOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ElectricEnergy"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"W","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q79813678"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:ElectricEnergy","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Active Energy","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ActivePower"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ElectricEnergy"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/InstantaneousPower"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ElectricEnergy"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ActivePower","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"\n  An $Active Power$ is, under periodic conditions, the mean value, taken over one period $T$, of the instantaneous power $p$. \n  In complex notation, $P = \\mathbf{Re} \\; \\underline{S}$, where $\\underline{S}$ is $\\textit{complex power}$.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/ExaW"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GigaW"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloW"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaW"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroW"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliW"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NanoW"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PetaW"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PicoW"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TeraJ-PER-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TeraW"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/W"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/eclassCode":[{"@value":"0173-1#Z4-BAJ277#005","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L2I0M1H0T-3D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/iec61360Code":[{"@value":"0112/2///62720#UAD003","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"http://www.electropedia.org/iev/iev.nsf/display?openform&ievref=131-11-42","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"https://cdd.iec.ch/cdd/iec62720/iec62720.nsf/ListsOfUnitsAllVersions/0112-2---62720%23UAD003","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"https://webstore.iec.ch/en/publication/60010","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexDefinition":[{"@value":"$P = \\frac{1}{T}\\int_{0}^{T} pdt$, where $T$ is the period and $p$ is instantaneous power.","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/specializationOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ElectricPower"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"P","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q12713281"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:ElectricPower","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Active Power","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/InstantaneousPower"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ElectricPower"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Activity","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"\n  $\\textit{Activity}$ is the number of decays per unit time of a radioactive sample,\n   the term used to characterise the number of nuclei which disintegrate in a radioactive substance per unit time. \n  Activity is usually measured in Becquerels ($Bq$), where 1 $Bq$ is 1 disintegration per second,\n   in honor of the scientist Henri Becquerel.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BQ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CI"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GigaBQ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloBQ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloCI"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaBQ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroBQ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroCI"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliBQ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliCI"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NanoBQ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PetaBQ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PicoCI"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TeraBQ"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/dbpediaMatch":[{"@value":"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Radioactive_decay","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/exactMatch":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/RadioactiveDecay"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Radioactivity"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T-1D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/iec61360Code":[{"@value":"0112/2///62720#UAD152","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://cdd.iec.ch/cdd/iec62720/iec62720.nsf/ListsOfUnitsAllVersions/0112-2---62720%23UAD152","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Radioactive_decay","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Radioactive_decay#Radioactive_decay_rates","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/isoNormativeReference":[{"@value":"http://www.iso.org/iso/catalogue_detail?csnumber=31895","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexDefinition":[{"@value":"\n  Variation $dN$ of number of nuclei $N$ in a particular energy state, \n   in a sample of a radionuclide, due to spontaneous nuclear transitions from this state during an infinitesimal time interval, \n   divided by its duration $dt$; thus: activity $A = -\\frac{dN}{dt}$.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/organizedUnder":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/StochasticProcess"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/siExactMatch":[{"@id":"https://si-digital-framework.org/quantities/ARRN"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"A","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q317949"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:Activity","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Activity","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/StochasticProcess"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ActivityCoefficient","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"An \"Activity Coefficient\" is a factor used in thermodynamics to account for deviations from ideal\n    behaviour in a mixture of chemical substances. In an ideal mixture, the interactions between each pair of chemical species are\n    the same (or more formally, the enthalpy change of solution is zero) and, as a result, properties of the mixtures can be\n    expressed directly in terms of simple concentrations or partial pressures of the substances present e.g. Raoult's law.\n    Deviations from ideality are accommodated by modifying the concentration by an activity coefficient.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/UNITLESS"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T0D1"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Activity_coefficient","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/isoNormativeReference":[{"@value":"http://www.iso.org/iso/catalogue_detail?csnumber=31894","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexDefinition":[{"@value":"$f_B = \\frac{\\lambda_B}{(\\lambda_B^*x_B)}$, where $\\lambda_B$ the absolute activity of substance $B$, $\\lambda_B^*$ is the absolute activity of the pure substance $B$ at the same temperature and pressure, and $x_B$ is the amount-of-substance fraction of substance $B$.","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"An \"Activity Coefficient\" is a factor used in thermodynamics to account for deviations from ideal\n    behaviour in a mixture of chemical substances. In an ideal mixture, the interactions between each pair of chemical species are\n    the same (or more formally, the enthalpy change of solution is zero) and, as a result, properties of the mixtures can be\n    expressed directly in terms of simple concentrations or partial pressures of the substances present e.g. Raoult's law.\n    Deviations from ideality are accommodated by modifying the concentration by an activity coefficient.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"f_B","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q745224"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:ActivityCoefficient","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Activity Coefficient","@language":"en"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ActivityConcentration","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"The \"Activity Concentration\", also known as volume activity, and activity density, is the ratio of the\n    activity of a sample containing radionuclides and the sample's volume.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BQ-PER-L"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BQ-PER-M3"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroBQ-PER-L"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliBQ-PER-L"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NanoBQ-PER-L"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PicoCI-PER-L"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L-3I0M0H0T-1D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://www.euronuclear.org/glossary/activity-concentration/","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/isoNormativeReference":[{"@value":"http://www.iso.org/iso/catalogue_detail?csnumber=31895","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexDefinition":[{"@value":"$c_A = \\frac{A}{V}$, where $A$ is the activity of a sample and $V$ is its volume.","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"The \"Activity Concentration\", also known as volume activity, and activity density, is the ratio of\n    the activity of a sample containing radionuclides and the sample's volume.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"c_A","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q423263"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:ActivityConcentration","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Activity Concentration","@language":"en"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ActivityRelatedByMass","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"$\\textit{Activity Related By Mass}$ is quantitative data of the radioactivity of the amount of a\n    radionuclide in a particular state of energy at a defined point in time, divided by the related mass of this quantity.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BQ-PER-KiloGM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CI-PER-KiloGM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloBQ-PER-KiloGM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaBQ-PER-KiloGM"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/eclassCode":[{"@value":"0173-1#Z4-BAJ342#005","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M-1H0T-1D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"quantitative Angabe der Radioaktivität einer Menge eines Radionuklids in einem bestimmten\n    Energiezustand zu einem gegebenen Zeitpunkt dividiert durch die zugehörige Masse dieser Menge\n  ","@language":"de"},{"@value":"quantitative data of the radioactivity of the amount of a radionuclide in a particular state of\n    energy at a defined point in time, divided by the related mass of this quantity\n  ","@language":"en"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/specializationOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/MassicActivity"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:MassicActivity","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Activity Related by Mass","@language":"en-us"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/MassicActivity"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ActivityThresholds","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"\"Activity Thresholds\" are threshold values of absorbed dose - the mean energy imparted by ionizing radiation to matter per unit mass - above which harmful (deterministic) effects occur. It has the dimension of specific energy and is expressed in gray.","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CentiGRAY"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GRAY"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloGRAY"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaGRAY"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroGRAY"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliGRAY"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliRAD_R"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NanoGRAY"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/RAD_R"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L2I0M0H0T-2D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"\"Activity Thresholds\" are threshold values of absorbed dose - the mean energy imparted by ionizing radiation to matter per unit mass - above which harmful (deterministic) effects occur. It has the dimension of specific energy and is expressed in gray.","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/specializationOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/AbsorbedDose"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:AbsorbedDose","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Activity Thresholds","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/AbsorbedDose"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Adaptation","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"\"Adaptation\" is the recovery of visual ability following exposure to light (dark adaptation), usually\n    measured in units of time.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MIN"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T1D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neural_adaptation#Visual","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/isoNormativeReference":[{"@value":"http://www.iso.org/iso/catalogue_detail?csnumber=43012","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"\"Adaptation\" is the recovery of visual ability following exposure to light (dark adaptation).","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/specializationOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Time"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:Adaptation","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Adaptation","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Time"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Admittance","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"\"Admittance\" is a measure of how easily a circuit or device will allow a current to flow. It is defined\n    as the inverse of the impedance ($Z$).\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DeciS"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloS"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MHO"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaS"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroMHO"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroS"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliS"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NanoS"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PicoS"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/S"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E2L-2I0M-1H0T3D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"http://www.electropedia.org/iev/iev.nsf/display?openform&ievref=131-12-51","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Admittance","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"https://webstore.iec.ch/en/publication/60010","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexDefinition":[{"@value":"$Y = \\frac{1}{Z}$, where $Z$ is impedance.","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexSymbol":[{"@value":"$Y$","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q214518"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:Admittance","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Admittance","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Impedance"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/AlphaDisintegrationEnergy","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"The \"Alpha Disintegration Energy\" is the sum of the kinetic energy of the $\\alpha$-particle produced in\n    the disintegration process and the recoil energy of the product atom in the reference frame in which the emitting nucleus is\n    at rest before its disintegration.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/AttoJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BTU_IT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BTU_TH"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CAL_IT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CAL_TH"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/ERG"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/EV"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/E_h"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/ExaJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FT-LB_F_Energy"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FT-PDL"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FemtoJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GigaEV"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GigaJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GigaW-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/J"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloBTU_IT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloBTU_TH"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloCAL"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloEV"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloW-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaBTU_IT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaEV"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaTOE"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaW-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NanoJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PetaJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PicoJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PlanckEnergy"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/QUAD"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/THERM_EC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/THERM_US"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/THM_EEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/THM_US"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TOE"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TeraJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TeraW-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TonEnergy"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/W-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/W-SEC"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L2I0M1H0T-2D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexSymbol":[{"@value":"$Q_a$","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/normativeReference":[{"@value":"http://www.iso.org/iso/catalogue_detail?csnumber=31895","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"The \"Alpha Disintegration Energy\" is the sum of the kinetic energy of the alpha-particle produced\n    in the disintegration process and the recoil energy of the product atom in the reference frame in which the emitting nucleus\n    is at rest before its disintegration.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/specializationOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Energy"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q98146025"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:Energy","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Alpha Disintegration Energy","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Energy"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Altitude","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"Altitude or height is defined based on the context in which it is used (aviation, geometry, geographical\n    survey, sport, and more). As a general definition, altitude is a distance measurement, usually in the vertical or \"up\"\n    direction, between a reference datum and a point or object. The reference datum also often varies according to the context.\n    [Wikipedia]\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/ANGSTROM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/AU"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BTU_IT-PER-LB_F"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CHAIN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CHAIN_US"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CentiM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DecaM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DeciM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FATH"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FT_US"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FUR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FemtoM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GAUGE_FR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GA_Charriere"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/HectoM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/IN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/LY"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MI"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MI_N"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MI_UK"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MI_US"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroIN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilLength"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliIN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NanoM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PARSEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PCA"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PicoM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PlanckLength"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/ROD"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/YD"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/ZOLL"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/dbpediaMatch":[{"@value":"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Altitude","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L1I0M0H0T0D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"Altitude or height is defined based on the context in which it is used (aviation, geometry,\n    geographical survey, sport, and more). As a general definition, altitude is a distance measurement, usually in the vertical or\n    \"up\" direction, between a reference datum and a point or object. The reference datum also often varies according to the\n    context. [Wikipedia]\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/specializationOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Length"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q190200"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:Length","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Altitude","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Length"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/AmbientPressure","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"The ambient pressure on an object is the pressure of the surrounding medium, such as a gas or liquid,\n    which comes into contact with the object. The SI unit of pressure is the pascal (Pa), which is a very small unit relative to\n    atmospheric pressure on Earth, so kilopascals ($kPa$) are more commonly used in this context.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/ATM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/ATM_T"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BAR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BARAD"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BARYE"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BAR_A"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CentiBAR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CentiM_H2O"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CentiM_H2O_4DEG_C"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CentiM_HG"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CentiM_HG_0DEG_C"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DYN-PER-CentiM2"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DecaPA"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DeciBAR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FT_H2O"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FT_H2O_39dot2DEG_F"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FT_HG"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GM_F-PER-CentiM2"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GigaPA"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/HectoBAR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/HectoPA"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/IN_H2O"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/IN_H2O_39dot2DEG_F"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/IN_H2O_60DEG_F"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/IN_HG"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/IN_HG_32DEG_F"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/IN_HG_60DEG_F"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KIP_F-PER-IN2"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloBAR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloGM-PER-M-SEC2"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloGM_F-PER-CentiM2"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloGM_F-PER-M2"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloGM_F-PER-MilliM2"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloLB_F-PER-IN2"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/v