"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/organizedUnder":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ForcePerLength"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"Quotient aus dem auf eine Fläche wirkenden, eine Verdrehung bzw. Abscherung verursachenden\n    Drehmoment dividiert durch diese Fläche\n  ","@language":"de"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:AreicTorque","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Areic Torque","@language":"en-us"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ForcePerLength"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Asset","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"An Asset is an economic resource owned by a business or company. Simply stated, assets are things of\n    value that can be readily converted into cash (although cash itself is also considered an asset).\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T0D1"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"An Asset is an economic resource owned by a business or company. Simply stated, assets are things\n    of value that can be readily converted into cash (although cash itself is also considered an asset).\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Asset","@language":"en"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/AtmosphericHydroxylationRate","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"A second order reaction rate constant that is a specific second order reaction rate constant that governs\n    the kinetics of an atmospheric, gas-phase reaction between hydroxyl radicals and an organic chemical.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CentiM3-PER-MOL-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/L-PER-MOL-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M3-PER-MOL-SEC"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A-1E0L3I0M0H0T-1D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"A second order reaction rate constant that is a specific second order reaction rate constant that\n    governs the kinetics of an atmospheric, gas-phase reaction between hydroxyl radicals and an organic chemical.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/specializationOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/SecondOrderReactionRateConstant"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:AtmosphericHydroxylationRate","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Atmospheric Hydroxylation Rate","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/SecondOrderReactionRateConstant"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/AtmosphericPressure","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"The pressure exerted by the weight of the air above it at any point on the earth's surface. At sea level\n    the atmosphere will support a column of mercury about $760 mm$ high. This decreases with increasing altitude. The stand