/AttoJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BTU_IT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BTU_TH"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CAL_IT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CAL_TH"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/ERG"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/EV"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/E_h"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/ExaJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FT-LB_F_Energy"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FT-PDL"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FemtoJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GigaEV"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GigaJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GigaW-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/J"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloBTU_IT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloBTU_TH"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloCAL"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloEV"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloW-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaBTU_IT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaEV"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaTOE"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaW-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NanoJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PetaJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PicoJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PlanckEnergy"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/QUAD"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/THERM_EC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/THERM_US"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/THM_EEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/THM_US"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TOE"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TeraJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TeraW-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TonEnergy"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/W-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/W-SEC"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L2I0M1H0T-2D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ionization_energy","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/normativeReference":[{"@value":"http://www.iso.org/iso/catalogue_detail?csnumber=31897","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"\"Donor Ionization Energy\" is the ionization energy of a donor.","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/specializationOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/IonizationEnergy"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"E_d","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q112958103"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:Energy","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Donor Ionization Energy","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/IonizationEnergy"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/AcceptorIonizationEnergy"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/DoseEquivalent","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"\"Dose Equivalent\" (former), or $\\textit{Equivalent Absorbed Radiation Dose}$, usually shortened to\n    $\\textit{Equivalent Dose}$, is a computed average measure of the radiation absorbed by a fixed mass of biological tissue,\n    that attempts to account for the different biological damage potential of different types of ionizing radiation. The\n    equivalent dose to a tissue is found by multiplying the absorbed dose, in gray, by a dimensionless \"quality factor\" $Q$,\n    dependent upon radiation type, and by another dimensionless factor $N$, dependent on all other pertinent factors. N depends\n    upon the part of the body irradiated, the time and volume over which the dose was spread, even the species of the subject.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroSV"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliR_man"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliSV"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NanoSV"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/REM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/R_man"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/SV"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/dbpediaMatch":[{"@value":"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Equivalent_dose","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/eclassCode":[{"@value":"0173-1#Z4-BAJ222#005","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L2I0M0H0T-2D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/iec61360Code":[{"@value":"0112/2///62720#UAD033","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://cdd.iec.ch/cdd/iec62720/iec62720.nsf/ListsOfUnitsAllVersions/0112-2---62720%23UAD033","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Equivalent_dose","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/isoNormativeReference":[{"@value":"http://www.iso.org/iso/catalogue_detail?csnumber=31895","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexDefinition":[{"@value":"At the point of interest in tissue, $H = DQ$, where $D$ is the absorbed dose and $Q$ is the quality factor at that point.","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/organizedUnder":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/SpecificEnergy"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/siExactMatch":[{"@id":"https://si-digital-framework.org/quantities/DOEQ"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"H","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q256106"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:DoseEquivalent","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Dose Equivalent","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/SpecificEnergy"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/DoseEquivalentQualityFactor","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"\"Dose Equivalent Quality Factor\" is a factor in the caculation and measurement of dose equivalent, by\n    which the absorbed dose is to be weighted in order to account for different biological effectiveness of radiations, for\n    radiation protection purposes.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/UNITLESS"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T0D1"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Equivalent_dose","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/isoNormativeReference":[{"@value":"http://www.iso.org/iso/catalogue_detail?csnumber=31895","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"\"Dose Equivalent Quality Factor\" is a factor in the caculation and measurement of dose equivalent,\n    by which the absorbed dose is to be weighted in order to account for different biological effectiveness of radiations, for\n    radiation protection purposes.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"Q","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q2122099"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:DoseEquivalentQualityFactor","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Dose Equivalent Quality Factor","@language":"en"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/DoseEquivalentRate","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroSV-PER-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroSV-PER-MIN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroSV-PER-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliSV-PER-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliSV-PER-MIN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliSV-PER-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NanoSV-PER-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NanoSV-PER-MIN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NanoSV-PER-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/SV-PER-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/SV-PER-MIN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/SV-PER-SEC"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L2I0M0H0T-3D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/iec61360Code":[{"@value":"0112/2///62720#UAD034","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://cdd.iec.ch/cdd/iec62720/iec62720.nsf/ListsOfUnitsAllVersions/0112-2---62720%23UAD034","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:DoseEquivalentRate","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Dose Equivalent Rate","@language":"en"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/DotsPerInch","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DPI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L-1I0M0H0T0D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/iec61360Code":[{"@value":"0112/2///62720#UAD255","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://cdd.iec.ch/cdd/iec62720/iec62720.nsf/ListsOfUnitsAllVersions/0112-2---62720%23UAD255","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/specializationOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/LineicResolution"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:DotsPerInch","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Dots per Inch","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/LineicResolution"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/DragCoefficient","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"In fluid dynamics, the drag coefficient is a dimensionless quantity that is used to quantify the drag or\n    resistance of an object in a fluid environment such as air or water.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/UNITLESS"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T0D1"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/organizedUnder":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Dimensionless"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"In fluid dynamics, the drag coefficient is a dimensionless quantity that is used to quantify the\n    drag or resistance of an object in a fluid environment such as air or water.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/qkdvDenominator":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L1I0M1H0T-2D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/qkdvNumerator":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L1I0M1H0T-2D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"C_D","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1778961"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:DragCoefficient","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Drag Coefficient","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Dimensionless"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/DragForce","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"In fluid dynamics, drag refers to forces which act on a solid object in the direction of the relative\n    fluid flow velocity. Unlike other resistive forces such as dry friction, which is nearly independent of velocity, drag forces\n    depend on velocity. Drag forces always decrease fluid velocity relative to the solid object in the fluid's path.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CentiN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DYN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DeciN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GM_F"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GigaN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KIP_F"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloGM-M-PER-SEC2"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloGM_F"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloLB_F"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloPOND"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/LB_F"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaLB_F"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/N"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NanoN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/OZ_F"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PDL"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/POND"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PlanckForce"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TON_F_US"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L1I0M1H0T-2D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"In fluid dynamics, drag refers to forces which act on a solid object in the direction of the\n    relative fluid flow velocity. Unlike other resistive forces such as dry friction, which is nearly independent of velocity,\n    drag forces depend on velocity. Drag forces always decrease fluid velocity relative to the solid object in the fluid's path.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/specializationOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Force"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"D or F_D","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:Force","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Drag Force","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Force"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/DryBulbTemperature","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"The temperature of air measured by a thermometer freely exposed to the air, but shielded from radiation.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DEG_C"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DEG_F"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H1T0D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"The temperature of air measured by a thermometer freely exposed to the air, but shielded from\n    radiation.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/specializationOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Temperature"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:DryBulbTemperature","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Dry Bulb Temperature","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Temperature"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/DryVolume","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"Dry measures are units of volume used to measure bulk commodities which are not gas or liquid. They are\n    typically used in agriculture, agronomy, and commodity markets to measure grain, dried beans, and dried and fresh fruit;\n    formerly also salt pork and fish. They are also used in fishing for clams, crabs, etc. and formerly for many other substances\n    (for example coal, cement, lime) which were typically shipped and delivered in a standardized container such as a barrel.  In\n    the original metric system, the unit of dry volume was the stere, but this is not part of the modern metric system; the liter\n    and the cubic meter ($m^{3}$) are now used. However, the stere is still widely used for firewood.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BBL_US_DRY"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BU_UK"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BU_US"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CORD"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GAL_US_DRY"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PINT_US_DRY"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PK_US_DRY"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/QT_US_DRY"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L3I0M0H0T0D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dry_measure","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/specializationOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Volume"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:DryVolume","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Dry Volume","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Volume"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/DutyCycle","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"A duty cycle or power cycle is the fraction of one period in which a signal or system is active.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FRACTION"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PERCENT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/UNITLESS"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T0D1"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duty_cycle","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexSymbol":[{"@value":"$\\alpha$","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/organizedUnder":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/DimensionlessRatio"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"A duty cycle or power cycle is the fraction of one period in which a signal or system is active.","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"α","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:DutyCycle","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Duty Cycle","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/DimensionlessRatio"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Duv","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"Duv is a metric that is short for Delta u,v (not to be confused with Delta u',v') and describes the\n    distance of a light color point from the black body curve.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/UNITLESS"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T0D1"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://www.waveformlighting.com/tech/calculate-duv-from-cie-1931-xy-coordinates","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"https://www1.eere.energy.gov/buildings/publications/pdfs/ssl/led-color-characteristics-factsheet.pdf","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"Duv is a metric that is short for Delta u,v (not to be confused with Delta u',v') and describes the\n    distance of a light color point from the black body curve.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:Duv","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Delta u,v","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/CorrelatedColorTemperature"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/DynamicFriction","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"Kinetic (or dynamic) friction occurs when two objects are moving relative to each other and rub together\n    (like a sled on the ground).\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"ht