e":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pressure","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"The force applied to a unit area of surface; measured in pascals (SI unit) or in dynes (cgs unit)","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"p","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:ForcePerArea","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Force per Area","@language":"en"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ForcePerAreaTime","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DeciBAR-PER-YR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/HectoPA-PER-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/LB_F-PER-IN2-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliW-PER-M2-NanoM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PA-PER-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PA-PER-MIN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PA-PER-SEC"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L-1I0M1H0T-3D0"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:ForcePerAreaTime","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Force per Area Time","@language":"en"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ForcePerElectricCharge","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"The electric field depicts the force exerted on other electrically charged objects by the electrically\n    charged particle the field is surrounding. The electric field is a vector field with SI units of newtons per coulomb ($N\n    C^{-1}$) or, equivalently, volts per metre ($V m^{-1}$ ). The SI base units of the electric field are $kg m s^{-3} A^{-1}$.\n    The strength or magnitude of the field at a given point is defined as the force that would be exerted on a positive test\n    charge of 1 coulomb placed at that point\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/N-PER-C"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E-1L1I0M1H0T-3D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electric_field","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:ForcePerElectricCharge","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Force per Electric Charge","@language":"en"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ForcePerLength","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DYN-PER-CentiM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloLB_F-PER-FT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloN-PER-M"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/LB_F-PER-FT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/LB_F-PER-IN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/LB_F-PER-YD"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliN-PER-M"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/N-PER-CentiM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/N-PER-M"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/N-PER-MilliM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PDL-PER-IN"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M1H0T-2D0"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:ForcePerLength","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Force per Length","@language":"en"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Frequency","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"\"Frequency\" is the number of occurrences of a repeating event per unit time. The repetition of the events\n    may be periodic (that is. the length of time between event repetitions is fixed) or aperiodic (i.e. the length of time between\n    event repetitions varies). Therefore, we distinguish between periodic and aperiodic frequencies. In the SI system, periodic\n    frequency is measured in hertz (Hz) or multiples of hertz, while aperiodic frequency is measured in becquerel (Bq).  In\n    spectroscopy, $\\nu$ is mostly used. Light passing through different media keeps its frequency, but not its wavelength or\n    wavenumber.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CYC-PER-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GigaHZ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/HZ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/HectoHZ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloHZ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaHZ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliHZ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PER-DAY"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PER-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PER-MIN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PER-MO"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PER-MilliSEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PER-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PER-WK"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PER-YR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PERCENT-PER-DAY"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PERCENT-PER-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PERCENT-PER-MO"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PPTH-PER-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PetaHZ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PlanckFrequency"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TeraHZ"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/dbpediaMatch":[{"@value":"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Frequency","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/eclassCode":[{"@value":"0173-1#Z4-BAJ257#004","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T-1D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/iec61360Code":[{"@value":"0112/2///62720#UAD056","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://cdd.iec.ch/cdd/iec62720/iec62720.nsf/ListsOfUnitsAllVersions/0112-2---62720%23UAD056","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexDefinition":[{"@value":"$f = 1/T$, where $T$ is a period.\n\nAlternatively,\n\n$\\nu = 1/T$","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexSymbol":[{"@value":"$\\nu, f$","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/organizedUnder":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/InverseTime"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/siExactMatch":[{"@id":"https://si-digital-framework.org/quantities/FREQ"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q11652"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:Frequency","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Frekuensi","@language":"ms"},{"@value":"Frekvence","@language":"cs"},{"@value":"Frequency","@language":"en"},{"@value":"Frequenz","@language":"de"},{"@value":"częstotliwość","@language":"pl"},{"@value":"frecuencia","@language":"es"},{"@value":"frecvență","@language":"ro"},{"@value":"frekans","@language":"tr"},{"@value":"frekvenca","@language":"sl"},{"@value":"frekvencia","@language":"hu"},{"@value":"frequentia","@language":"la"},{"@value":"frequenza","@language":"it"},{"@value":"frequência","@language":"pt"},{"@value":"fréquence","@language":"fr"},{"@value":"Συχνότητα","@language":"el"},{"@value":"Частота","@language":"ru"},{"@value":"Честота","@language":"bg"},{"@value":"תדירות","@language":"he"},{"@value":"التردد لدى نظام الوحدات الدولي","@language":"ar"},{"@value":"بسامد","@language":"fa"},{"@value":"आवृत्ति","@language":"hi"},{"@value":"周波数","@language":"ja"},{"@value":"频率","@language":"zh"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/InverseTime"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Friction","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"\"Friction\" is the force of two surfaces In contact, or the force of a medium acting on a moving object\n    (that is air on an aircraft). When contacting surfaces move relative to each other, the friction between the two objects\n    converts kinetic energy into thermal energy.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CentiN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DYN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DeciN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GM_F"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GigaN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KIP_F"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloGM-M-PER-SEC2"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloGM_F"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloLB_F"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloPOND"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/LB_F"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaLB_F"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/N"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NanoN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/OZ_F"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PDL"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/POND"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PlanckForce"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TON_F_US"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/dbpediaMatch":[{"@value":"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Friction","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L1I0M1H0T-2D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"http://wiki.answers.com/Q/What_is_the_symbol_of_friction","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Friction","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"\"Friction\" is the force of two surfaces In contact, or the force of a medium acting on a moving\n    object (that is air on an aircraft). When contacting surfaces move relative to each other, the friction between the two\n    objects converts kinetic energy into thermal energy.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/specializationOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Force"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q82580"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:Force","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qud