on use. It can either\n    indicate how \"tall\" something is, or how \"high up\" it is.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/abbreviation":[{"@value":"height","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/ANGSTROM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/AU"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BTU_IT-PER-LB_F"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CHAIN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CHAIN_US"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CentiM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DecaM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DeciM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FATH"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FT_US"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FUR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FemtoM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GAUGE_FR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GA_Charriere"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/HectoM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/IN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/LY"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MI"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MI_N"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MI_UK"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MI_US"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroIN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilLength"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliIN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NanoM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PARSEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PCA"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PicoM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PlanckLength"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/ROD"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/YD"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/ZOLL"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/dbpediaMatch":[{"@value":"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Height","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L1I0M0H0T0D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Height","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/normativeReference":[{"@value":"http://www.iso.org/iso/catalogue_detail?csnumber=43012","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"\"Height\" is the measurement of vertical distance, but has two meanings in common use. It can either\n    indicate how \"tall\" something is, or how \"high up\" it is.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/specializationOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Length"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"h","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q208826"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:Length","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Height","@language":"en"},{"@value":"Höhe","@language":"de"},{"@value":"Ketinggian","@language":"ms"},{"@value":"Výška","@language":"cs"},{"@value":"altezza","@language":"it"},{"@value":"altura","@language":"es"},{"@value":"altura","@language":"pt"},{"@value":"hauteur","@language":"fr"},{"@value":"yükseklik","@language":"tr"},{"@value":"Înălțime","@language":"ro"},{"@value":"высота","@language":"ru"},{"@value":"ارتفاع","@language":"fa"},{"@value":"高度","@language":"zh"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Length"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/HelmholtzEnergy","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"$\\textit{Helmholtz Energy}$ is one of the potentials are used to measure energy changes in systems as\n    they evolve from an initial state to a final state. The potential used depends on the constraints of the system, such as\n    constant temperature or pressure. $\\textit{Internal Energy}$ is the internal energy of the system, $\\textit{Enthalpy}$ is\n    the internal energy of the system plus the energy related to pressure-volume work, and Helmholtz and Gibbs free energy are the\n    energies available in a system to do useful work when the temperature and volume or the pressure and temperature are fixed,\n    respectively. The name $\\textit{Helmholz Free Energy}$ is also used.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/AttoJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BTU_IT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BTU_TH"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CAL_IT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CAL_TH"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/ERG"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/EV"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/E_h"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/ExaJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FT-LB_F_Energy"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FT-PDL"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FemtoJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GigaEV"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GigaJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GigaW-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/J"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloBTU_IT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloBTU_TH"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloCAL"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloEV"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloW-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaBTU_IT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaEV"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaTOE"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaW-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NanoJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PetaJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PicoJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PlanckEnergy"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/QUAD"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/THERM_EC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/THERM_US"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/THM_EEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/THM_US"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TOE"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TeraJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TeraW-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TonEnergy"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/W-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/W-SEC"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L2I0M1H0T-2D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"http://en.citizendium.org/wiki/Thermodynamics","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/isoNormativeReference":[{"@value":"http://www.iso.org/iso/catalogue_detail?csnumber=31890","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexDefinition":[{"@value":"$H = U - T \\cdot S$, where $U$ is internal energy, $T$ is thermodynamic temperature and $S$ is entropy.","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/specializationOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Energy"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"A","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:Energy","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Energía de Helmholtz","@language":"es"},{"@value":"Helmholtz Energy","@language":"en"},{"@value":"Helmholtz enerjisi","@language":"tr"},{"@value":"Helmholtzova volná energie","@language":"cs"},{"@value":"Prosta energija","@language":"sl"},{"@value":"Tenaga Helmholtz","@language":"ms"},{"@value":"energia libera di Helmholz","@language":"it"},{"@value":"energia livre de Helmholtz","@language":"pt"},{"@value":"energia swobodna","@language":"pl"},{"@value":"freie Energie","@language":"de"},{"@value":"énergie libre","@language":"fr"},{"@value":"свободная энергия Гельмгольца","@language":"ru"},{"@value":"انرژی آزاد هلمولتز","@language":"fa"},{"@value":"طاقة هلمهولتز الحرة","@language":"ar"},{"@value":"ヘルムホルツの自由エネルギー","@language":"ja"},{"@value":"亥姆霍兹自由能","@language":"zh"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Energy"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Enthalpy"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/GibbsEnergy"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/InternalEnergy"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel":[{"@value":" Helmholtz fonksiyonu","@language":"tr"},{"@value":"Helmholtz function","@language":"en"},{"@value":"Helmholtz-Energie","@language":"de"},{"@value":"Helmholtz-Funktion","@language":"de"},{"@value":"fungsi Helmholtz","@language":"ms"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Energy"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/HenrysLawVolatilityConstant","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"A quantity kind that is a proportionality constant that relates the partial pressure of a gas above a\n    liquid and the concentration of the gas dissolved in the liquid.  The numerator contains the gaseous concentration and the\n    denominator contains the liquid concentration.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/ATM-M3-PER-MOL"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A-1E0L2I0M1H0T-2D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"A quantity kind that is a proportionality constant that relates the partial pressure of a gas above\n    a liquid and the concentration of the gas dissolved in the liquid.  The numerator contains the gaseous concentration and the\n    denominator contains the liquid concentration.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:HenrysLawVolatilityConstant","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Henry's Law Volatility Constant","@language":"en"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/HoleDensity","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"\"Hole Density\" is the number of holes per volume in a valence band.","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NUM-PER-L"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NUM-PER-M3"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NUM-PER-MicroL"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NUM-PER-MilliL"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NUM-PER-MilliM3"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NUM-PER-NanoL"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NUM-PER-PicoL"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L-3I0M0H0T0D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/normativeReference":[{"@value":"http://www.iso.org/iso/catalogue_detail?csnumber=31897","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"\"Hole Density\" is the number of holes per volume in a valence band.","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/specializationOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/NumberDensity"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"p","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q105971101"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:NumberDensity","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Hole Density","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/NumberDensity"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/HorizontalVelocity","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"Component of a projectile's velocity, which acts parallel to the ground and does not lift the projectile\n    in the air.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CentiM-PER-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CentiM-PER-KiloYR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CentiM-PER-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CentiM-PER-YR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FT-PER-DAY"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FT-PER-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FT-PER-MIN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FT-PER-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GigaHZ-M"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/IN-PER-MIN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/IN-PER-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/IN-PER-YR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloM-PER-DAY"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloM-PER-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloM-PER-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M-PER-DAY"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M-PER-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M-PER-MIN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M-PER-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M-PER-YR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MI-PER-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MI-PER-MIN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MI-PER-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MI_N-PER-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MI_N-PER-MIN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroM-PER-MIN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroM-PER-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliM-PER-DAY"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliM-PER-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliM-PER-MIN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliM-PER-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliM-PER-YR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/YD-PER-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/YD-PER-MIN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/YD-PER-SEC"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L1I0M0H0T-1D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"Component of a projectile's velocity, which acts parallel to the ground and does not lift the\n    projectile in the air.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/specializationOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/LinearVelocity"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Velocity"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"V_{X}","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:LinearVelocity","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"},{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:Velocity","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Horizontal Velocity","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/LinearVelocity"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Velocity"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/HydraulicPermeability","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"Permeability is a property of porous materials that is an indication of the ability for fluids (gas or\n    liquid) to flow through them. Fluids can more easily flow through a material with high permeability than one with low\n    permeability. The permeability of a medium is related to the porosity, but also to the shapes of the pores in the medium and\n    their level of connectedness.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CentiM2"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DARCY"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DeciM2"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FT2"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/IN2"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloM2"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M2"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MIL_Circ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroM2"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliDARCY"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliM2"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NanoM2"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/baseCGSUnitDimensions":[{"@value":"$cm^2$","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/baseSIUnitDimensions":[{"@value":"$m^2$","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/dbpediaMatch":[{"@value":"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Permeability_(Earth_sciences)","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L2I0M0H0T0D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Permeability_(Earth_sciences)","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/organizedUnder":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Area"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"Permeability is a property of porous materials that is an indication of the ability for fluids (gas\n    or liquid) to flow through them. Fluids can more easily flow through a material with high permeability than one with low\n    permeability. The permeability of a medium is related to the porosity, but also to the shapes of the pores in the medium and\n    their level of connectedness.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:HydraulicPermeability","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Hydraulic Permeability","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel":[{"@value":"Fluid Permeability","@language":"en"},{"@value":"Permeability","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Area"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/HyperfineStructureQuantumNumber","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"The \"Hyperfine Structure Quantum Number\" is a quantum number of an atom describing inclination of the\n    nuclear spin with respect to a quantization axis given by the magnetic field produced by the orbital electrons.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/UNITLESS"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T0D1"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hyperfine_structure","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quantum_number","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/isoNormativeReference":[{"@value":"http://www.iso.org/iso/catalogue_detail?csnumber=31894","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/organizedUnder":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/QuantumNumber"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"The \"Hyperfine Structure Quantum Number\" is a quantum number of an atom describing inclination of\n    the nuclear spin with respect to a quantization axis given by the magnetic field produced by the orbital electrons.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"F","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q97577449"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:HyperfineStructureQuantumNumber","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Hyperfine Structure Quantum Number","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/QuantumNumber"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/INERT-MASS","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"The sum of the vehicle dry mass, residual fluids and gasses, personnel and personnel provisions, and\n    cargo.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/deprecated":[{"@value":"true","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/deprecatedInVersion":[{"@value":"3.2.0","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M1H0T0D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"The sum of the vehicle dry mass, residual fluids and gasses, personnel and personnel provisions,\n    and cargo.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Inert Mass","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Mass"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/IgnitionIntervalTime","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliSEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/SEC"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T1D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/specializationOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Time"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:IgnitionIntervalTime","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Ignition Interval Time","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Time"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Illuminance","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"Illuminance is the total luminous flux incident on a surface, per unit area. It is a measure of the\n    intensity of the incident light, wavelength-weighted by the luminosity function to correlate with human brightness perception.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/LM-PER-FT2"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/LM-PER-M2"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/LUX"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PHOT"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/dbpediaMatch":[{"@value":"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Illuminance","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/eclassCode":[{"@value":"0173-1#Z4-BAJ201#001","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L-2I1M0H0T0D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/iec61360Code":[{"@value":"0112/2///62720#UAD062","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://cdd.iec.ch/cdd/iec62720/iec62720.nsf/ListsOfUnitsAllVersions/0112-2---62720%23UAD062","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Illuminance","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexDefinition":[{"@value":"$E_v = \\frac{d\\Phi}{dA}$, where $d\\Phi$ is the luminous flux incident on an element of the surface with area $dA$.","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"Illuminance is the total luminous flux incident on a surface, per unit area. It is a measure of the\n    intensity of the incident light, wavelength-weighted by the luminosity function to correlate with human brightness perception.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/siExactMatch":[{"@id":"https://si-digital-framework.org/quantities/ILLU"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/specializationOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/LuminousFluxPerArea"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q194411"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:LuminousFluxPerArea","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Beleuchtungsstärke","@language":"de"},{"@value":"Illuminance","@language":"en"},{"@value":"Intenzita osvětlení","@language":"cs"},{"@value":"Pencahayaan","@language":"ms"},{"@value":"aydınlanma şiddeti","@language":"tr"},{"@value":"illuminamento","@language":"it"},{"@value":"iluminamento","@language":"pt"},{"@value":"iluminare","@language":"ro"},{"@value":"luminosidad","@language":"es"},{"@value":"megvilágítás","@language":"hu"},{"@value":"natężenie oświetlenia","@language":"pl"},{"@value":"osvetljenost","@language":"sl"},{"@value":"éclairement lumineux","@language":"fr"},{"@value":"Осветеност","@language":"bg"},{"@value":"Освещённость","@language":"ru"},{"@value":"הארה (שטף ליחידת שטח)","@language":"he"},{"@value":"شدة الضوء","@language":"ar"},{"@value":"شدت روشنایی","@language":"fa"},{"@value":"प्रदीपन","@language":"hi"},{"@value":"照度","@language":"ja"},{"@value":"照度","@language":"zh"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel":[{"@value":"éclairement","@language":"fr"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/LuminousFluxPerArea"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Impedance","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"\"Impedance\" is the measure of the opposition that a circuit presents to the passage of a current when a\n    voltage is applied. In quantitative terms, it is the complex ratio of the voltage to the current in an alternating current\n    (AC) circuit. Impedance extends the concept of resistance to AC circuits, and possesses both magnitude and phase, unlike\n    resistance, which has only magnitude. When a circuit is driven with direct current (DC), there is no distinction between\n    impedance and resistance; the latter can be thought of as impedance with zero phase angle.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/OHM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PlanckImpedance"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/dbpediaMatch":[{"@value":"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Electrical_impedance","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E-2L2I0M1H0T-3D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"http://www.electropedia.org/iev/iev.nsf/display?openform&ievref=131-12-43","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electrical_impedance","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"https://webstore.iec.ch/en/publication/60010","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexDefinition":[{"@value":"$\\underline{Z} = \\underline{U} / \\underline{I}$, where $\\underline{U}$ is the voltage phasor and $\\underline{I}$ is the electric current phasor.","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexSymbol":[{"@value":"$\\underline{Z}$","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/organizedUnder":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Resistance"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"\"Impedance\" is the measure of the opposition that a circuit presents to the passage of a current\n    when a voltage is applied. In quantitative terms, it is the complex ratio of the voltage to the current in an alternating\n    current (AC) circuit. Impedance extends the concept of resistance to AC circuits, and possesses both magnitude and phase,\n    unlike resistance, which has only magnitude. When a circuit is driven with direct current (DC), there is no distinction\n    between impedance and resistance; the latter can be thought of as impedance with zero phase angle.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q179043"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:Impedance","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Impedance","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ElectricCurrentPhasor"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/VoltagePhasor"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Resistance"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Impulse","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"product of force and time","@language":"en"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GM-CentiM-PER-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloGM-CentiM-PER-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/LB-FT-PER-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/LB-IN-PER-SEC"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/eclassCode":[{"@value":"0173-1#Z4-BAJ241#004","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"},{"@value":"0173-1#Z4-BAJ262#004","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L1I0M1H0T-1D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/iec61360Code":[{"@value":"0112/2///62720#UAD063","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://cdd.iec.ch/cdd/iec62720/iec62720.nsf/ListsOfUnitsAllVersions/0112-2---62720%23UAD063","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"Produkt aus Kraft und Zeit","@language":"de"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:Impulse","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Impulse","@language":"en-us"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Incidence","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"In epidemiology, incidence is the rate at which new cases of a given medical condition occur in a\n    population: the number of new occurrences counted per unit time. The same quantity as quantitykind:IncidenceRate, from a\n    different source vocabulary (IEC 61360). For the dimensionless fraction of a population affected within a specified period,\n    see quantitykind:IncidenceProportion.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NUM-PER-YR"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/exactMatch":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/IncidenceRate"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T-1D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/iec61360Code":[{"@value":"0112/2///62720#UAD064","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://cdd.iec.ch/cdd/iec62720/iec62720.nsf/ListsOfUnitsAllVersions/0112-2---62720%23UAD064","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Incidence_(epidemiology)","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/organizedUnder":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/CountRate"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"In epidemiology, incidence is the rate at which new cases of a given medical condition occur in a\n    population: the number of new occurrences counted per unit time. The same quantity as quantitykind:IncidenceRate, from a\n    different source vocabulary (IEC 61360). For the dimensionless fraction of a population affected within a specified period,\n    see quantitykind:IncidenceProportion.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/qkdvDenominator":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T1D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/qkdvNumerator":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T0D1"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:Incidence","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Incidence","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/IncidenceProportion"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/CountRate"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/IncidenceProportion","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"Incidence proportion (also known as cumulative incidence) is the number of new cases within a specified\n    time period divided by the size of the population initially at risk. For example, if a population initially contains 1,000\n    non-diseased persons and 28 develop a condition over two years of observation, the incidence proportion is 28 cases per 1,000\n    persons per two years, i.e. 2.8% per two years.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FRACTION"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PERCENT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/UNITLESS"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T0D1"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cumulative_incidence","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Incidence_(epidemiology)","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/organizedUnder":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/DimensionlessRatio"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"Incidence proportion (also known as cumulative incidence) is the number of new cases within a\n    specified time period divided by the size of the population initially at risk. For example, if a population initially contains\n    1,000 non-diseased persons and 28 develop a condition over two years of observation, the incidence proportion is 28 cases per\n    1,000 persons per two years, i.e. 2.8% per two years.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/qkdvDenominator":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T0D1"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/qkdvNumerator":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T0D1"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q217690"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:IncidenceProportion","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Incidence Proportion","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/IncidenceRate"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/DimensionlessRatio"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/IncidenceRate","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"The incidence rate is a measure of the frequency with which a disease or other incident occurs over a\n    specified time period. It is also known as the incidence density rate or person-time incidence rate, when the denominator is\n    the combined person-time of the population at risk (the sum of the time duration of exposure across all persons exposed)\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NUM-PER-YR"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/exactMatch":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Incidence"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T-1D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Incidence_(epidemiology)","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/organizedUnder":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/CountRate"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"The incidence rate is a measure of the frequency with which a disease or other incident occurs over\n    a specified time period. It is also known as the incidence density rate or person-time incidence rate, when the denominator is\n    the combined person-time of the population at risk (the sum of the time duration of exposure across all persons exposed)\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/qkdvDenominator":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T1D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/qkdvNumerator":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T0D1"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:IncidenceRate","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Incidence Rate","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/IncidenceProportion"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/CountRate"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Inductance","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"\"Inductance\" is an electromagentic quantity that characterizes a circuit's resistance to any change of\n    electric current; a change in the electric current through induces an opposing electromotive force (EMF). Quantitatively,\n    inductance is proportional to the magnetic flux per unit of electric current.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/H"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/H_Ab"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/H_Stat"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloH"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroH"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliH"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NanoH"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PicoH"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/dbpediaMatch":[{"@value":"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Inductance","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E-2L2I0M1H0T-2D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/iec61360Code":[{"@value":"0112/2///62720#UAD065","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"http://www.electropedia.org/iev/iev.nsf/display?openform&ievref=131-12-19","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"https://cdd.iec.ch/cdd/iec62720/iec62720.nsf/ListsOfUnitsAllVersions/0112-2---62720%23UAD065","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"https://webstore.iec.ch/en/publication/60010","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexDefinition":[{"@value":"$L =\\frac{\\Psi}{I}$, where $I$ is an electric current in a thin conducting loop, and $\\Psi$ is the linked flux caused by that electric current.","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"\"Inductance\" is an electromagentic quantity that characterizes a circuit's resistance to any change\n    of electric current; a change in the electric current through induces an opposing electromotive force (EMF). Quantitatively,\n    inductance is proportional to the magnetic flux per unit of electric current.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/siExactMatch":[{"@id":"https://si-digital-framework.org/quantities/ELIN"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"L","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q177897"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:Inductance","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Inductance électrique","@language":"fr"},{"@value":"Inductance","@language":"en"},{"@value":"Indukstans","@language":"ms"},{"@value":"Induktivität","@language":"de"},{"@value":"Indukčnost","@language":"cs"},{"@value":"inductancia","@language":"es"},{"@value":"inductantia","@language":"la"},{"@value":"inductanță","@language":"ro"},{"@value":"indukcyjność","@language":"pl"},{"@value":"induktivitás","@language":"hu"},{"@value":"induktivnost","@language":"sl"},{"@value":"induttanza","@language":"it"},{"@value":"indutância","@language":"pt"},{"@value":"İndüktans","@language":"tr"},{"@value":"Индуктивност","@language":"bg"},{"@value":"Индуктивность","@language":"ru"},{"@value":"השראות","@language":"he"},{"@value":"القاوری","@language":"fa"},{"@value":"المحاثة (التحريض)","@language":"ar"},{"@value":"प्रेरकत्व","@language":"hi"},{"@value":"インダクタンス・誘導係数","@language":"ja"},{"@value":"电感","@language":"zh"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/MutualInductance"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel":[{"@value":"Induktiviti","@language":"ms"},{"@value":"inductivity","@language":"en"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/InductanceBasedTimeConstant","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"The inductance-based time constant, $\\tau = L/R$, of an RL circuit is the time taken for the current to\n    reach a fraction $1 - 1/e$ (about 63%) of its final value after a step change in the applied voltage. It is the ratio of the\n    inductance $L$ to the resistance $R$ and has the dimension of time, expressed in seconds.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/H-PER-KiloOHM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/H-PER-OHM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroH-PER-KiloOHM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroH-PER-OHM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroSEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliH-PER-KiloOHM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliH-PER-OHM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliSEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/SEC"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/exactMatch":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ResistanceBasedInductance"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T1D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/iec61360Code":[{"@value":"0112/2///62720#UAD198","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://cdd.iec.ch/cdd/iec62720/iec62720.nsf/ListsOfUnitsAllVersions/0112-2---62720%23UAD198","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"The inductance-based time constant, tau = L/R, of an RL circuit is the time taken for the current to\n    reach a fraction 1 - 1/e (about 63%) of its final value after a step change in the applied voltage. It is the ratio of the\n    inductance L to the resistance R and has the dimension of time, expressed in seconds.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/specializationOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Time"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:InductanceBasedTimeConstant","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Inductance Based Time Constant","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Time"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/InfiniteMultiplicationFactor","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"The \"Infinite Multiplication Factor\" is the multiplication factor for an infinite medium or for an\n    infinite repeating lattice.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/UNITLESS"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T0D1"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Four_factor_formula","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/isoNormativeReference":[{"@value":"http://www.iso.org/iso/catalogue_detail?csnumber=31895","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexSymbol":[{"@value":"$k_\\infty$","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"The \"Infinite Multiplication Factor\" is the multiplication factor for an infinite medium or for an\n    infinite repeating lattice.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/specializationOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/MultiplicationFactor"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q99440487"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:MultiplicationFactor","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Infinite Multiplication Factor","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/MultiplicationFactor"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/EffectiveMultiplicationFactor"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/InformationContent","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"The information content (or self-information) I(x) of an outcome x is a measure of the information gained\n    when x occurs, defined as the logarithm of the reciprocal of its probability: I(x) = log(1/p(x)). The value depends on the\n    base of the logarithm, which fixes the unit — base 2 gives the shannon (Sh), base e the nat, and base 10 the hartley (Hart).\n    It is the per-outcome quantity whose expectation over a distribution is the information entropy.\n  ","@language":"en"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BAN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/HART"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NAT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/SHANNON"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/eclassCode":[{"@value":"0173-1#Z4-BAJ463#001","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"},{"@value":"0173-1#Z4-BAJ468#001","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"},{"@value":"0173-1#Z4-BAJ469#001","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T0D1"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/iec61360Code":[{"@value":"0112/2///62720#UAD066","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://cdd.iec.ch/cdd/iec62720/iec62720.nsf/ListsOfUnitsAllVersions/0112-2---62720%23UAD066","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"The information content (or self-information) I(x) of an outcome x is a measure of the information\n    gained when x occurs, defined as the logarithm of the reciprocal of its probability: I(x) = log(1/p(x)). The value depends on\n    the base of the logarithm, which fixes the unit — base 2 gives the shannon (Sh), base e the nat, and base 10 the hartley\n    (Hart). It is the per-outcome quantity whose expectation over a distribution is the information entropy.\n  ","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:InformationContent","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"},{"@value":"ECLASS models the choice of logarithm base as three separate quantities, so all three of its codes map to this\n    one quantity kind. Where a single ECLASS code is required, select the one matching the unit in which the quantity is\n    expressed: BAJ463 (base 2) for unit:SHANNON, BAJ468 (base 10) for unit:HART, and BAJ469 (base e) for unit:NAT. QUDT follows\n    IEC CDD UAD066, which lists the shannon, the hartley and the natural unit of information as three units of a single quantity,\n    leaving the base to be carried by the unit. See qudt-public-repo issue 1410.\n  ","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Information Content","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/InformationEntropy"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/InformationContentExpressedAsALogarithmToBase10","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"I(xi) as the information content I(xi) of a result xi (e.g. the occurrence of a character xi) is the\n    common logarithm of the reciprocal of the probability p(xi) of its occurrence, i.e.: l(x) lg 1/p(x) Hart, where p(x) is the\n    probability of the event x\n  ","@language":"en"}],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/isReplacedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/InformationContent"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/deprecated":[{"@value":"true","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/deprecatedInVersion":[{"@value":"3.5.0","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/eclassCode":[{"@value":"0173-1#Z4-BAJ468#001","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T0D1"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"(xi) als der Informationsgehalt I(xi) eines Ergebnisses xi (z. B. das Auftreten eines Zeichens xi)\n    ist der dekatischer Logarithmus des Kehrwertes der Wahrscheinlichkeit p (xi) für sein eintreten, also: l(x) lg 1/p(x) Hart,\n    dabei ist p(x) die Wahrscheinlichkeit des Ereignisses x\n  ","@language":"de"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Information Content Expressed as a Logarithm to Base 10","@language":"en-us"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/InformationContentExpressedAsALogarithmToBase2","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"I(xi) as the information content I(xi) of a result xi (e.g. the occurrence of a character xi) is the\n    binary logarithm of the reciprocal of the probability p(xi) of its occurrence, i.e.: l(x) lb 1/p(x) Sh, where p(x) is the\n    probability of the event x\n  ","@language":"en"}],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/isReplacedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/InformationContent"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/deprecated":[{"@value":"true","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/deprecatedInVersion":[{"@value":"3.5.0","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/eclassCode":[{"@value":"0173-1#Z4-BAJ463#001","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T0D1"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"I(xi) als der Informationsgehalt I(xi) eines Ergebnisses xi (z. B. das Auftreten eines Zeichens xi)\n    ist der binäre Logarithmus des Kehrwertes der Wahrscheinlichkeit p (xi) für sein eintreten, also: l(x) = lb 1/p(x) Sh, dabei\n    ist p(x) die Wahrscheinlichkeit des Ereignisses x\n  ","@language":"de"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Information Content Expressed as a Logarithm to Base 2","@language":"en-us"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/InformationContentExpressedAsALogarithmToBaseE","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"I(xi) as the information content I(xi) of a result xi (e.g. the occurrence of a character xi) is the\n    natural logarithm of the reciprocal of the probability p(xi) of its occurrence, i.e.: l(x) ln 1/p(x) nat, where p(x) is the\n    probability of the event x\n  ","@language":"en"}],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/isReplacedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/InformationContent"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/deprecated":[{"@value":"true","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/deprecatedInVersion":[{"@value":"3.5.0","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/eclassCode":[{"@value":"0173-1#Z4-BAJ469#001","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T0D1"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"I(xi) als der Informationsgehalt I(xi) eines Ergebnisses xi (z. B. das Auftreten eines Zeichens xi)\n    ist der natürliche Logarithmus des Kehrwertes der Wahrscheinlichkeit p (xi) für sein eintreten, also: l(x) = ln 1/p(x) nat,\n    dabei ist p(x) die Wahrscheinlichkeit des Ereignisses x\n  ","@language":"de"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Information Content Expressed as a Logarithm to Base e","@language":"en-us"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/InformationEntropy","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"Information Entropy is a concept from information theory. It tells how much information there is in an\n    event. In general, the more uncertain or random the event is, the more information it will contain. The concept of information\n    entropy was created by a mathematician. He was named Claude Elwood Shannon. It has applications in many areas, including\n    lossless data compression, statistical inference, cryptography and recently in other disciplines as biology, physics or\n    machine learning.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BAN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/ERLANG"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/HART"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NAT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/SHANNON"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T0D1"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"http://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Information_entropy","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/organizedUnder":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Dimensionless"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"Information Entropy is a concept from information theory. It tells how much information there is in\n    an event. In general, the more uncertain or random the event is, the more information it will contain. The concept of\n    information entropy was created by a mathematician. He was named Claude Elwood Shannon. It has applications in many areas,\n    including lossless data compression, statistical inference, cryptography and recently in other disciplines such as biology, physics\n    or machine learning.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q204570"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:InformationEntropy","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Information Entropy","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Dimensionless"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/InformationFlowRate","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"The rate at which information content (Shannon entropy) is conveyed by a source or over a channel:\n    information content per unit time, measured in shannons, nats, or hartleys per second according to the logarithm base. It is\n    an information-theoretic quantity, distinct from quantitykind:DataRate, which counts raw bits transferred per second\n    regardless of their information content; by the source coding theorem the information flow rate of a channel is at most its\n    data rate.\n  ","@language":"en"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/HART-PER-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NAT-PER-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/SHANNON-PER-SEC"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/eclassCode":[{"@value":"0173-1#Z4-BAJ464#001","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"},{"@value":"0173-1#Z4-BAJ470#001","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"},{"@value":"0173-1#Z4-BAJ471#001","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T-1D0"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:InformationFlowRate","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"},{"@value":"ECLASS models the choice of logarithm base as three separate quantities, so all three of its codes map to this\n    one quantity kind, with the base carried by the unit. Where a single ECLASS code is required, select the one matching the\n    unit in which the quantity is expressed: BAJ464 (base 2) for unit:SHANNON-PER-SEC, BAJ470 (base 10) for unit:HART-PER-SEC,\n    and BAJ471 (base e) for unit:NAT-PER-SEC. ECLASS also qualifies these as a \"median\" information flow; that is a statistical\n    property of a particular measurement rather than of the quantity kind, so it is not reflected here. See qudt-public-repo\n    issue 1410.\n  ","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Information Flow Rate","@language":"en"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/InitialExpansionRatio","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M-PER-DEG_C-M"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliM-PER-DEG_C-M"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PER-DEG_F"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PER-K"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PER-MegaK"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PPM-PER-K"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PPTM-PER-K"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H-1T0D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/specializationOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ExpansionRatio"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:ExpansionRatio","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Initial Expansion Ratio","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ExpansionRatio"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/InitialVehicleMass","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/AMU"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CARAT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CWT_LONG"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CWT_SHORT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CentiGM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DRAM_UK"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DRAM_US"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DWT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DecaGM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DeciGM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DeciTONNE"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DeciTON_Metric"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/EarthMass"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FemtoGM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GM_Carbon"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GM_DRY"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GM_Nitrogen"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GRAIN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/HectoGM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/Hundredweight_UK"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/Hundredweight_US"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloGM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloLB"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloTONNE"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloTON_Metric"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/LB"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/LB_M"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/LB_T"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/LunarMass"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MOMME_Pearl"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MOMME_Textile"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaGM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaTON"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaTONNE"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroGM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliGM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NanoGM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/OZ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/OZ_M"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/OZ_TROY"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PENNYWEIGHT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PFUND"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PicoGM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PlanckMass"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/Quarter_UK"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/SLUG"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/SolarMass"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/Stone_UK"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TON"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TONNE"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TON_Assay"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TON_LONG"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TON_Metric"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TON_SHORT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TON_UK"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TON_US"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/U"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M1H0T0D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/specializationOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Mass"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"M_{o}","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:Mass","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Initial Vehicle Mass","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Mass"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/InitialVelocity","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"The velocity of a moving body at starting; especially, the velocity of a projectile as it leaves the\n    mouth of a firearm from which it is discharged.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CentiM-PER-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CentiM-PER-KiloYR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CentiM-PER-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CentiM-PER-YR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FT-PER-DAY"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FT-PER-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FT-PER-MIN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FT-PER-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GigaHZ-M"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/IN-PER-MIN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/IN-PER-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/IN-PER-YR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloM-PER-DAY"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloM-PER-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloM-PER-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M-PER-DAY"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M-PER-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M-PER-MIN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M-PER-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M-PER-YR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MI-PER-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MI-PER-MIN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MI-PER-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MI_N-PER-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MI_N-PER-MIN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroM-PER-MIN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroM-PER-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliM-PER-DAY"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliM-PER-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliM-PER-MIN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliM-PER-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliM-PER-YR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/YD-PER-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/YD-PER-MIN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/YD-PER-SEC"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L1I0M0H0T-1D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"The velocity of a moving body at starting; especially, the velocity of a projectile as it leaves\n    the mouth of a firearm from which it is discharged.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/specializationOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/LinearVelocity"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Velocity"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"V_{i}","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:LinearVelocity","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"},{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:Velocity","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Initial Velocity","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/LinearVelocity"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Velocity"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/InstantaneousPower","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"For a two-terminal element or a two-terminal circuit with terminals A and B, $\\textit{Instantaneous\n    Power}$ is the product of the voltage $u_{AB}$ between the terminals and the electric current i in the element or circuit: $$p\n    = u_{AB} \\cdot i$$ Where $u_{AB}$ is the line integral of the electric field strength from A to B, and where the electric\n    current in the element or circuit is taken positive if its direction is from A to B and negative in the opposite case. $$$$\n    For an n-terminal circuit, it is the sum of the instantaneous powers relative to the n - 1 pairs of terminals when one of the\n    terminals is chosen as a common terminal for the pairs. $$$$ For a polyphase element, it is the sum of the instantaneous\n    powers in all phase elements of a polyphase element. $$$$ For a polyphase line consisting of m line conductors and one neutral\n    conductor, it is the sum of the m instantaneous powers expressed for each line conductor by the product of the polyphase\n    line-to-neutral voltage and the corresponding line current.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/ExaW"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GigaW"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloW"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaW"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroW"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliW"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NanoW"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PetaW"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PicoW"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TeraJ-PER-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TeraW"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/W"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L2I0M1H0T-3D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"http://www.electropedia.org/iev/iev.nsf/display?openform&ievref=131-11-30","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"http://www.electropedia.org/iev/iev.nsf/display?openform&ievref=131-11-31","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"http://www.electropedia.org/iev/iev.nsf/display?openform&ievref=141-02-14","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"http://www.electropedia.org/iev/iev.nsf/display?openform&ievref=141-03-10","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Power","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"https://webstore.iec.ch/en/publication/60010","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexDefinition":[{"@value":"$p = ui$, where $u$ is instantaneous voltage and $i$ is instantaneous electric current.","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/specializationOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ElectricPower"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"p","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:ElectricPower","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Instantaneous Power","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ElectricPower"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/InternalConversionFactor","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"The \"InternalConversionFactor\" describes the rate of internal conversion. It is the ratio of the number\n    of internal conversion electrons to the number of gamma quanta emitted by the radioactive atom in a given transition.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/UNITLESS"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T0D1"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Internal_conversion_coefficient","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/isoNormativeReference":[{"@value":"http://www.iso.org/iso/catalogue_detail?csnumber=31895","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"The \"InternalConversionFactor\" describes the rate of internal conversion. It is the ratio of the\n    number of internal conversion electrons to the number of gamma quanta emitted by the radioactive atom in a given transition.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"a","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q6047819"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:InternalConversionFactor","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Internal Conversion Factor","@language":"en"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/InternalEnergy","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"\"Internal Energy\" is simply its energy. \"internal\" refers to the fact that some energy contributions are\n    not considered. For instance, when the total system is in uniform motion, it has kinetic energy. This overall kinetic energy\n    is never seen as part of the internal energy; one could call it external energy. Or, if the system is at constant non-zero\n    height above the surface the Earth, it has constant potential energy in the gravitational field of the Earth. Gravitational\n    energy is only taken into account when it plays a role in the phenomenon of interest, for instance in a colloidal suspension,\n    where the gravitation influences the up- downward motion of the small particles comprising the colloid. In all other cases,\n    gravitational energy is assumed not to contribute to the internal energy; one may call it again external energy.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/abbreviation":[{"@value":"int-energy","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/AttoJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BTU_IT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BTU_TH"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CAL_IT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CAL_TH"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/ERG"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/EV"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/E_h"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/ExaJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FT-LB_F_Energy"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FT-PDL"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FemtoJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GigaEV"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GigaJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GigaW-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/J"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloBTU_IT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloBTU_TH"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloCAL"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloEV"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloW-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaBTU_IT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaEV"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaTOE"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaW-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NanoJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PetaJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PicoJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PlanckEnergy"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/QUAD"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/THERM_EC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/THERM_US"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/THM_EEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/THM_US"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TOE"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TeraJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TeraW-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TonEnergy"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/W-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/W-SEC"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/dbpediaMatch":[{"@value":"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Internal_energy","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/exactMatch":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ThermodynamicEnergy"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L2I0M1H0T-2D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"http://en.citizendium.org/wiki/Internal_energy","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexDefinition":[{"@value":"For a closed thermodynamic system, $\\Delta U = Q + W$, where $Q$ is amount of heat transferred to the system and $W$ is work done on the system provided that no chemical reactions occur.","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/normativeReference":[{"@value":"http://www.iso.org/iso/catalogue_detail?csnumber=31890","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"\"Internal Energy\" is simply its energy. \"internal\" refers to the fact that some energy\n    contributions are not considered. For instance, when the total system is in uniform motion, it has kinetic energy. This\n    overall kinetic energy is never seen as part of the internal energy; one could call it external energy. Or, if the system is\n    at constant non-zero height above the surface the Earth, it has constant potential energy in the gravitational field of the\n    Earth. Gravitational energy is only taken into account when it plays a role in the phenomenon of interest, for instance in a\n    colloidal suspension, where the gravitation influences the up- downward motion of the small particles comprising the colloid.\n    In all other cases, gravitational energy is assumed not to contribute to the internal energy; one may call it again external\n    energy.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/specializationOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Energy"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"U","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q180241"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:Energy","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Internal Energy","@language":"en"},{"@value":"Notranja energija","@language":"sl"},{"@value":"Tenaga dalaman","@language":"ms"},{"@value":"energia interna","@language":"it"},{"@value":"energia interna","@language":"pt"},{"@value":"energia wewnętrzna","@language":"pl"},{"@value":"energie internă","@language":"ro"},{"@value":"energía interna","@language":"es"},{"@value":"innere Energie","@language":"de"},{"@value":"vnitřní energie","@language":"cs"},{"@value":"énergie interne","@language":"fr"},{"@value":"İç enerji","@language":"tr"},{"@value":"внутренняя энергия","@language":"ru"},{"@value":"انرژی درونی","@language":"fa"},{"@value":"طاقة داخلية","@language":"ar"},{"@value":"आन्तरिक ऊर्जा","@language":"hi"},{"@value":"内能","@language":"zh"},{"@value":"内部エネルギー","@language":"ja"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Energy"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Enthalpy"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/GibbsEnergy"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/HelmholtzEnergy"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel":[{"@value":"energia termodinamica","@language":"it"},{"@value":"tenaga termodinamik","@language":"ms"},{"@value":"thermodynamic energy","@language":"en"},{"@value":"thermodynamische Energie","@language":"de"},{"@value":"énergie thermodynamique","@language":"fr"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Energy"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/IntinsicCarrierDensity","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"\"Intrinsic Carrier Density\" is proportional to electron and hole densities.","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/isReplacedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/IntrinsicCarrierDensity"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/deprecated":[{"@value":"true","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/deprecatedInVersion":[{"@value":"3.2.0","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L-3I0M0H0T0D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexDefinition":[{"@value":"$np = n_i^2$, where $n$ is electron density and $p$ is hole density.","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/normativeReference":[{"@value":"http://www.iso.org/iso/catalogue_detail?csnumber=31897","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"\"Intrinsic Carrier Density\" is proportional to electron and hole densities.","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"n_i","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1303188"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Intrinsic Carrier Density","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/NumberDensity"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/IntrinsicCarrierDensity","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"\"Intrinsic Carrier Density\" is proportional to electron and hole densities.","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NUM-PER-L"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NUM-PER-M3"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NUM-PER-MicroL"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NUM-PER-MilliL"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NUM-PER-MilliM3"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NUM-PER-NanoL"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NUM-PER-PicoL"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L-3I0M0H0T0D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexDefinition":[{"@value":"$np = n_i^2$, where $n$ is electron density and $p$ is hole density.","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/normativeReference":[{"@value":"http://www.iso.org/iso/catalogue_detail?csnumber=31897","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"\"Intrinsic Carrier Density\" is proportional to electron and hole densities.","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/specializationOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/NumberDensity"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"n_i","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1303188"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:NumberDensity","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Intrinsic Carrier Density","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/NumberDensity"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/InverseAmountOfSubstance","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PER-MOL"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/exactMatch":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/MolarDensity"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A-1E0L0I0M0H0T0D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q93421670"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:InverseAmountOfSubstance","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Inverse Amount of Substance","@language":"en"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/InverseArea","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PER-IN2"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PER-M-NanoM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PER-M2"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L-2I0M0H0T0D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"A quantity with dimension of inverse area (L⁻²), used for generic inverse-area units such as microscopic cross-sections and attenuation coefficients that do not imply a count of discrete particles.","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:InverseArea","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Inverse Area","@language":"en"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/InverseEnergy","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PER-J"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PER-KiloVA-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PER-VA-SEC"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/exactMatch":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ReciprocalEnergy"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L-2I0M-1H0T2D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/iec61360Code":[{"@value":"0112/2///62720#UAD156","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://cdd.iec.ch/cdd/iec62720/iec62720.nsf/ListsOfUnitsAllVersions/0112-2---62720%23UAD156","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:InverseEnergy","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Inverse Energy","@language":"en"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/InverseEnergy_Squared","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/isReplacedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/InverseSquareEnergy"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/deprecated":[{"@value":"true","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/deprecatedInVersion":[{"@value":"3.1.3","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L-4I0M-2H0T4D0"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Inverse Square Energy","@language":"en"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/InverseLength","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"Reciprocal length or inverse length is a measurement used in several branches of science and mathematics.\n    As the reciprocal of length, common units used for this measurement include the reciprocal metre or inverse metre ($m^{-1}$),\n    the reciprocal centimetre or inverse centimetre ($cm^{-1}$), and, in optics, the dioptre.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KY"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M-PER-HA"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M-PER-M2"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MESH"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PER-ANGSTROM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PER-CentiM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PER-KiloM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PER-M"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PER-MicroM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PER-MilliM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PER-NanoM"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PER-PicoM"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L-1I0M0H0T0D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reciproc