value":"Thermal Coefficient of Linear Expansion","@language":"en-us"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ExpansionRatio"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ThermalConductance","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"This quantity is also called \"Heat Transfer Coefficient\".","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloVA-PER-K"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroVA-PER-K"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliVA-PER-K"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/VA-PER-K"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/W-PER-K"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/eclassCode":[{"@value":"0173-1#Z4-BAJ408#004","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L2I0M1H-1T-3D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/iec61360Code":[{"@value":"0112/2///62720#UAD189","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://cdd.iec.ch/cdd/iec62720/iec62720.nsf/ListsOfUnitsAllVersions/0112-2---62720%23UAD189","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thermal_insulation","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/isoNormativeReference":[{"@value":"http://www.iso.org/iso/catalogue_detail?csnumber=31890","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexDefinition":[{"@value":"$G = 1/R$, where $R$ is \"Thermal Resistance\"","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"This quantity is also called \"Heat Transfer Coefficient\".","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"G","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q17176562"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:ThermalConductance","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Thermal Conductance","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/CoefficientOfHeatTransfer"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ThermalConductivity","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"In physics, thermal conductivity, $k$ (also denoted as $\\lambda$), is the property of a material's\n    ability to conduct heat. It appears primarily in Fourier's Law for heat conduction and is the areic heat flow rate divided by\n    temperature gradient.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BTU_IT-FT-PER-FT2-HR-DEG_F"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BTU_IT-IN-PER-FT2-HR-DEG_F"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BTU_IT-IN-PER-FT2-SEC-DEG_F"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BTU_IT-IN-PER-HR-FT2-DEG_F"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BTU_IT-IN-PER-SEC-FT2-DEG_F"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BTU_IT-PER-SEC-FT-DEG_R"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BTU_TH-FT-PER-FT2-HR-DEG_F"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BTU_TH-FT-PER-HR-FT2-DEG_F"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BTU_TH-IN-PER-FT2-HR-DEG_F"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BTU_TH-IN-PER-FT2-SEC-DEG_F"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CAL_IT-PER-SEC-CentiM-K"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CAL_TH-PER-CentiM-SEC-DEG_C"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CAL_TH-PER-SEC-CentiM-K"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloCAL-PER-CentiM-SEC-DEG_C"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloCAL_IT-PER-HR-M-DEG_C"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloW-PER-M-DEG_C"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloW-PER-M-K"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/W-PER-M-DEG_C"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/W-PER-M-K"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/dbpediaMatch":[{"@value":"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Thermal_conductivity","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/eclassCode":[{"@value":"0173-1#Z4-BAJ407#005","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/expression":[{"@value":"$thermal-k$","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L1I0M1H-1T-3D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/iec61360Code":[{"@value":"0112/2///62720#UAD380","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://cdd.iec.ch/cdd/iec62720/iec62720.nsf/ListsOfUnitsAllVersions/0112-2---62720%23UAD380","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thermal_conductivity","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexDefinition":[{"@value":"$\\lambda = \\frac{\\varphi}{T}$, where $\\varphi$ is areic heat flow rate and $T$ is temperature gradient.","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexSymbol":[{"@value":"$\\lambda$","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/siExactMatch":[{"@id":"https://si-digital-framework.org/quantities/TCON"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q487005"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:ThermalConductivity","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Thermal Conductivity","@language":"en"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ThermalDiffusionFactor","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"Thermal diffusion is a phenomenon in which a temperature gradient in a mixture of fluids gives rise to a\n    flow of one constituent relative to the mixture as a whole. in the context of the equation that describes thermal diffusion,\n    the \"Thermal Diffusion Factor\" is .\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/UNITLESS"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T0D1"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"http://www.thermopedia.com/content/1189/","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/isoNormativeReference":[{"@value":"http://www.iso.org/iso/catalogue_detail?csnumber=31894","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexDefinition":[{"@value":"$\\alpha_T = \\frac{k_T}{(x_A x_B)}$, where $k_T$ is the thermal diffusion ratio, and $x_A$ and $x_B$ are the local amount-of-substance fractions of the two substances $A$ and $B$.","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexSymbol":[{"@value":"$\\alpha_T$","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"Thermal diffusion is a phenomenon in which a temperature gradient in a mixture of fluids gives rise\n    to a flow of one constituent relative to the mixture as a whole. in the context of the equation that describes thermal\n    diffusion, the \"Thermal Diffusion Factor\" is .\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q96249629"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:ThermalDiffusionFactor","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Thermal Diffusion Factor","@language":"en"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ThermalDiffusionRatio","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"The \"Thermal Diffusion Ratio\" is proportional to the product of the component concentrations.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/UNITLESS"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T0D1"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"http://www.thermopedia.com/content/1189/","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/isoNormativeReference":[{"@value":"http://www.iso.org/iso/catalogue_detail?csnumber=31894","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexDefinition":[{"@value":"In a steady state of a binary mixture in which thermal diffusion occurs, $grad x_B  = -(\\frac{k_T}{T}) grad T$, where $x_B$ is the amount-of-substance fraction of the heavier substance $B$, and $T$ is the local thermodynamic temperature.","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"The \"Thermal Diffusion Ratio\" is proportional to the product of the component concentrations.","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"k_T","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q96249433"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:ThermalDiffusionRatio","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Thermal Diffusion Ratio","@language":"en"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ThermalDiffusionRatioCoefficient","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M2-PER-SEC"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L2I0M0H0T-1D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"http://www.thermopedia.com/content/1189/","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/isoNormativeReference":[{"@value":"http://www.iso.org/iso/catalogue_detail?csnumber=31894","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexDefinition":[{"@value":"$D_T  = kT \\cdot D$, where $k_T$ is the thermal diffusion ratio, and $D$ is the diffusion coefficient.","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"D_T","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q96249751"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:ThermalDiffusionRatioCoefficient","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Thermal Diffusion Coefficient","@language":"en"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ThermalDiffusivity","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"In heat transfer analysis, thermal diffusivity (usually denoted $\\alpha$ but $a$, $\\kappa$,$k$, and $D$\n    are also used) is the thermal conductivity divided by density and specific heat capacity at constant pressure. The formula is:\n    $\\alpha = {k \\over {\\rho c_p}}$, where k is thermal conductivity ($W/(\\mu \\cdot K)$), $\\rho$ is density ($kg/m^{3}$),\n    and $c_p$ is specific heat capacity ($\\frac{J}{(kg \\cdot K)}$) .The denominator $\\rho c_p$, can be considered the\n    volumetric heat capacity ($\\frac{J}{(m^{3} \\cdot K)}$).\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CentiM2-PER-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FT2-PER-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M2-PER-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliM2-PER-SEC"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/dbpediaMatch":[{"@value":"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Thermal_diffusivity","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L2I0M0H0T-1D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/iec61360Code":[{"@value":"0112/2///62720#UAD031","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://cdd.iec.ch/cdd/iec62720/iec62720.nsf/ListsOfUnitsAllVersions/0112-2---62720%23UAD031","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thermal_diffusivity","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexDefinition":[{"@value":"$a = \\frac{\\lambda}{\\rho   c_\\rho}$, where $\\lambda$ is thermal conductivity, $\\rho$ is mass density and $c_\\rho$ is specific heat capacity at constant pressure.","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexSymbol":[{"@value":"$\\alpha$","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/organizedUnder":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/AreaPerTime"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"a","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q3381809"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:ThermalDiffusivity","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Thermal Diffusivity","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/AreaPerTime"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ThermalEfficiency","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"Thermal efficiency is a dimensionless performance measure of a thermal device such as an internal\n    combustion engine, a boiler, or a furnace. The input to the device is heat, or the heat-content of a fuel that is consumed.\n    The desired output is mechanical work, or heat, or possibly both.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FRACTION"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PERCENT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/UNITLESS"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/dbpediaMatch":[{"@value":"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Thermal_efficiency","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T0D1"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/isoNormativeReference":[{"@value":"http://www.iso.org/iso/catalogue_detail?csnumber=31890","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"Thermal efficiency is a dimensionless performance measure of a thermal device such as an internal\n    combustion engine, a boiler, or a furnace. The input to the device is heat, or the heat-content of a fuel that is consumed.\n    The desired output is mechanical work, or heat, or possibly both.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/qkdvDenominator":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L2I0M1H0T-2D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/qkdvNumerator":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L2I0M1H0T-2D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/specializationOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Efficiency"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1452104"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:ThermalEfficiency","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Thermal Efficiency","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Efficiency"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ThermalEnergy","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"\"Thermal Energy\" is the portion of the thermodynamic or internal energy of a system that is responsible\n    for the temperature of the system. From a macroscopic thermodynamic description, the thermal energy of a system is given by\n    its constant volume specific heat capacity C(T), a temperature coefficient also called thermal capacity, at any given absolute\n    temperature (T): $U_{thermal} = C(T) \\cdot T$.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BTU_39DEG_F"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BTU_59DEG_F"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BTU_60DEG_F"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BTU_IT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BTU_MEAN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BTU_TH"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CAL_15DEG_C"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CAL_20DEG_C"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CAL_IT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CAL_MEAN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CAL_TH"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GigaJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/J"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloBTU_IT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloBTU_TH"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloCAL"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloCAL_IT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloCAL_Mean"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloCAL_TH"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaBTU_IT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NanoJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PicoJ"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/THERM_EC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/THERM_US"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/THM_EEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/THM_US"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TON_FG-HR"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/dbpediaMatch":[{"@value":"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Thermal_energy","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L2I0M1H0T-2D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/iec61360Code":[{"@value":"0112/2///62720#UAD191","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://cdd.iec.ch/cdd/iec62720/iec62720.nsf/ListsOfUnitsAllVersions/0112-2---62720%23UAD191","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thermal_energy","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/specializationOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Energy"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q209233"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:ThermalEnergy","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Thermal Energy","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Energy"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ThermalEnergyLength","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BTU_IT-FT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BTU_IT-IN"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L3I0M1H0T-2D0"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:ThermalEnergyLength","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Thermal Energy Length","@language":"en"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ThermalExpansionCoefficient","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"The \"Thermal Expansion Coefficient\" is a measure of the thermal expansion coefficient of a material,\n    which expresses its elongation (as a ratio) per temperature difference. It is usually measured in 1/K. A positive elongation\n    per (positive) rise of temperature is expressed by a positive value.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M-PER-DEG_C-M"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliM-PER-DEG_C-M"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PER-DEG_C"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PERCENT-PER-DEG_C"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PPM-PER-K"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PPTM-PER-K"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H-1T0D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/iec61360Code":[{"@value":"0112/2///62720#UAD188","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://cdd.iec.ch/cdd/iec62720/iec62720.nsf/ListsOfUnitsAllVersions/0112-2---62720%23UAD188","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"https://standards.buildingsmart.org/IFC/DEV/IFC4_3/RC2/HTML/link/ifcthermalexpansioncoefficientmeasure.htm","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"The \"Thermal Expansion Coefficient\" is a measure of the thermal expansion coefficient of a\n    material, which expresses its elongation (as a ratio) per temperature difference. It is usually measured in 1/K. A positive\n    elongation per (positive) rise of temperature is expressed by a positive value.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/specializationOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ExpansionRatio"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:ThermalExpansionCoefficient","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Thermal Expansion Coefficient","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ExpansionRatio"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ThermalInertia","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/J-PER-M2-SEC0dot5-K"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E-2L2I0M1H-1T-2dot5D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thermal_inertia","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"Thermal inertia is a term used to describe the observed delays in a body's temperature response\n    during heat transfers\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:ThermalInertia","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Measurement Unit of Thermal Inertia","@language":"en"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ThermalInsulance","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"$\\textit{Thermal Insulance}$ is the reduction of heat transfer (the transfer of thermal energy between\n    objects of differing temperature) between objects in thermal contact or in range of radiative influence. In building\n    technology, this quantity is often called $\\textit{Thermal Resistance}$, with the symbol $R$.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CLO"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DEG_F-HR-FT2-PER-BTU_IT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DEG_F-HR-FT2-PER-BTU_TH"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FT2-HR-DEG_F-PER-BTU_IT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M2-HR-DEG_C-PER-KiloCAL_IT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M2-K-PER-W"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/exactMatch":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ThermalInsulation"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M-1H1T3D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/iec61360Code":[{"@value":"0112/2///62720#UAD192","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://cdd.iec.ch/cdd/iec62720/iec62720.nsf/ListsOfUnitsAllVersions/0112-2---62720%23UAD192","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thermal_insulation","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexDefinition":[{"@value":"$M = 1/K$, where $K$ is \"Coefficient of Heat Transfer\"","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"M","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q2596212"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:ThermalInsulance","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Thermal Insulance","@language":"en"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/CoefficientOfHeatTransfer"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ThermalInsulation","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"temperature difference between two surfaces divided by areic heat flow rate in the direction of the\n    temperature gradient\n  ","@language":"en"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CLO"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DEG_F-HR-FT2-PER-BTU_IT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DEG_F-HR-FT2-PER-BTU_TH"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FT2-HR-DEG_F-PER-BTU_IT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M2-HR-DEG_C-PER-KiloCAL_IT"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M2-K-PER-W"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/eclassCode":[{"@value":"0173-1#Z4-BAJ404#004","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/exactMatch":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ThermalInsulance"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M-1H1T3D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"Temperaturdifferenz zwischen zwei Oberflächen dividiert durch den flächenbezogenen Wärmestrom in\n    der Richtung des Temperaturgradienten\n  ","@language":"de"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment":[{"@value":"Applicable units are those of quantitykind:ThermalInsulation","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Thermal Insulation","@language":"en-us"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ThermalPower","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BAR-L-PER-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BAR-M3-PER-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BTU_IT-PER-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/BTU_IT-PER-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/ERG-PER-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/ExaJ-PER-SEC"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/ExaW"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FT-LB_F-PER-HR"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/u