meability","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"The moisture transmission rate of a material is referred to as its \"permeability\".","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/isReplacedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/VapourPermeability"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/deprecated":[{"@value":"true","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/deprecatedInVersion":[{"@value":"3.1.3","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T1D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://users.encs.concordia.ca/~raojw/crd/essay/essay000287.html","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"https://www.designingbuildings.co.uk/wiki/Vapour_Permeability","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"The moisture transmission rate of a material is referred to as its \"permeability\".","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Vapour Permeability","@language":"en"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/VaporPermeance","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"A material's \"permeance\", is dependent on thickness much like the R-value in heat transmission. Dividing\n    the permeability of a material by its thickness gives the material's permeance. Permeance is the number that should be used to\n    compare various products in regard to moisture transmission resistance.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/isReplacedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/VapourPermeance"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/deprecated":[{"@value":"true","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/deprecatedInVersion":[{"@value":"3.1.3","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L-1I0M0H0T1D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://users.encs.concordia.ca/~raojw/crd/essay/essay000287.html","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"https://www.designingbuildings.co.uk/wiki/Vapour_Permeability","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"A material's \"permeance\", is dependent on thickness much like the R-value in heat transmission.\n    Dividing the permeability of a material by its thickness gives the material's permeance. Permeance is the number that should\n    be used to compare various products in regard to moisture transmission resistance.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Vapour Permeance","@language":"en"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/VaporPressure","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"A pressure that is the one exerted by a substance vapour in thermodynamic equilibrium with either its\n    solid or liquid phase at a given temperature in a closed system.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/isReplacedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/VapourPressure"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/deprecated":[{"@value":"true","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/deprecatedInVersi