ical body.  Or, the product of the mass of a\n    body and the acceleration acting on a body.  In a dynamic situation, the weight can be a multiple of that under resting\n    conditions. Weight also varies on other planets in accordance with their gravity.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/CentiN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DYN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DeciN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GM_F"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/GigaN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KIP_F"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloGM-M-PER-SEC2"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloGM_F"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloLB_F"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloPOND"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/LB_F"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaLB_F"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/N"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NanoN"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/OZ_F"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PDL"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/POND"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PlanckForce"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TON_F_US"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/dbpediaMatch":[{"@value":"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Weight","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L1I0M1H0T-2D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Weight","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"The force with which a body is attracted toward an astronomical body.  Or, the product of the mass\n    of a body and the acceleration acting on a bod