 as the mass of a given substance (chemical element or chemical compound) divided by its amount of substance. It\n    is a physical property of a given substance. However, for historical reasons, molar masses are almost always expressed in\n    $g/mol$. As an example, the molar mass of water is approximately: $18.01528(33) \\; g/mol$.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableSystem":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/SI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/conversionMultiplier":[{"@value":"1.0","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/conversionMultiplierSN":[{"@value":"1.0E0","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/derivedCoherentUnitOfSystem":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/SI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/expression":[{"@value":"$kg mol^{-1}$","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A-1E0L0I0M1H0T0D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasFactorUnit":[{"@id":"_:n3-2171"},{"@id":"_:n3-2172"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasQuantityKind":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/MolarMass"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasReciprocalUnit":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MOL-PER-KiloGM"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/iec61360Code":[{"@value":"0112/2///62720#UAA628","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://cdd.iec.ch/cdd/iec62720/iec62720.nsf/Units/0112-2---62720%23UAA628","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"kg/mol","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/ucumCode":[{"@value":"kg.mol-1","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/UCUMcs"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/uneceCommonCode":[{"@value":"D74","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#str