elling as used by the International Bureau of Weights and Measures) or\n    millimeter (American spelling) (SI unit symbol mm) is a unit of length in the metric system, equal to one thousandth of a\n    metre, which is the SI base unit of length. It is equal to 1000 micrometres or 1000000 nanometres. A millimetre is equal to\n    exactly 5/127 (approximately 0.039370) of an inch.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableSystem":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/CGS"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/CGS-EMU"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/CGS-GAUSS"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/SI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/conversionMultiplier":[{"@value":"0.001","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/conversionMultiplierSN":[{"@value":"1.0E-3","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/dbpediaMatch":[{"@value":"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Millimetre","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/expression":[{"@value":"$mm$","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L1I0M0H0T0D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasQuantityKind":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Length"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/iec61360Code":[{"@value":"0112/2///62720#UAA862","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://cdd.iec.ch/cdd/iec62720/iec62720.nsf/Units/0112-2---62720%23UAA862","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Millimetre?oldid=493032457","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/prefix":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/prefix/Milli"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/scalingOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M"}],"http: