 of the partial pressure of water vapor to the equilibrium vapor\n    pressure of water at a given temperature, expressed as a percentage.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableSystem":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/ASU"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/CGS"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/CGS-EMU"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/CGS-ESU"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/CGS-GAUSS"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/IMPERIAL"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/PLANCK"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/SI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/conversionMultiplier":[{"@value":"0.01","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/conversionMultiplierSN":[{"@value":"1.0E-2","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T0D1"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasQuantityKind":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/RelativeHumidity"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"Percent relative humidity is the ratio of the partial pressure of water vapor to the equilibrium\n    vapor pressure of water at a given temperature, expressed as a percentage.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/scalingOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/UNITLESS"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"%RH","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/unitForQuantityKind":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/RelativeHumidity"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/unit"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Percent Relative Humidity","@language":"en"},{"@value":"Percent Relative Humidity","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PERMEABILITY_EM_REL","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/Unit"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"Relative permeability, denoted by the symbol $\\mu _T$, is the ratio of the permeability of a specific\n    medium to the permeability of free space $\\mu _0$\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableSystem":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/CGS-EMU"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/conversionMultiplier":[{"@value":"1.0","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/conversionMultiplierSN":[{"@value":"1.0E0","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/dbpediaMatch":[{"@value":"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Relative_permeability","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/derivedUnitOfSystem":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/CGS-EMU"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T0D1"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasQuantityKind":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ElectromagneticPermeabilityRatio"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Relative_permeability","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/latexSymbol":[{"@value":"$\\mu\\,T$","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"μₜ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/ucumCode":[{"@value":"[mu_0]","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/UCUMcs"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/unitForQuantityKind":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ElectromagneticPermeabilityRatio"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/unit"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Relative Electromagnetic Permeability","@language":"en"},{"@value":"Relative Electromagnetic Permeability","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PERMEABILITY_REL","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/Unit"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"In multiphase flow in porous media, the relative permeability of a phase is a dimensionless measure of\n    the effective permeability of that phase. It is the ratio of the effective permeability of that phase to the absolute\n    permeability. It can be viewed as an adaptation of Darcy's law to multiphase flow. For two-phase flow in porous media given\n    steady-state conditions, we can write where is the flux, is the pressure drop, is the viscosity.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableSystem":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/CGS-EMU"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/conversionMultiplier":[{"@value":"0.00000125663706","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/conversionMultiplierSN":[{"@value":"1.25663706E-6","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/dbpediaMatch":[{"@value":"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Relative_permeability","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/derivedUnitOfSystem":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/CGS-EMU"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T0D1"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasQuantityKind":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/PermeabilityRatio"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Relative_permeability","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/scalingOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/UNITLESS"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"kᵣ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/unitForQuantityKind":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/PermeabilityRatio"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/unit"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Relative Permeability","@language":"en"},{"@value":"Relative Permeability","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PERMILLE","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/Unit"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"\"Permille\" is a unit for 'Dimensionless Ratio' analogous to Percent, but per thousand rather than per\n    hundred.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableSystem":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/ASU"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/CGS"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/CGS-EMU"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/CGS-ESU"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/CGS-GAUSS"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/IMPERIAL"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/PLANCK"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/SI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/conversionMultiplier":[{"@value":"0.001","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/conversionMultiplierSN":[{"@value":"1.0E-3","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T0D1"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasQuantityKind":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/DimensionlessRatio"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/MoleFraction"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/VoltageImbalance"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/VolumeStrain"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Per_mille","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/omUnit":[{"@id":"http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/percent"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/scalingOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/UNITLESS"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"‰","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/udunitsCode":[{"@value":"permille","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/uneceCommonCode":[{"@value":"J13","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/unitForQuantityKind":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/DimensionlessRatio"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/MoleFraction"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/VoltageImbalance"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/VolumeStrain"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/wikidataMatch":[{"@id":"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q11229"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/unit"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Permille","@language":"en"},{"@value":"Permille","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PERMILLE-PER-PSI","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/Unit"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"thousandth divided by the composed unit for pressure (pound-force per square inch)","@type":"http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/conversionMultiplier":[{"@value":"0.0000001450377377302092151542410279511941","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/conversionMultiplierSN":[{"@value":"1.450377377302092151542410279511941E-7","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L1I0M-1H0T2D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasFactorUnit":[{"@id":"_:n3-4682"},{"@id":"_:n3-4683"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasQuantityKind":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Compressibility"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/InversePressure"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/iec61360Code":[{"@value":"0112/2///62720#UAA016","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://cdd.iec.ch/cdd/iec62720/iec62720.nsf/Units/0112-2---62720%23UAA016","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"thousandth divided by the composed unit for pressure (pound-force per square inch)","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"‰/psi","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/ucumCode":[{"@value":"‰.[psi]-1","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/UCUMcs"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/uneceCommonCode":[{"@value":"J12","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/unitForQuantityKind":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Compressibility"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/InversePressure"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/unit"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Permille per Psi","@language":"en"},{"@value":"Permille per Psi","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PERMITTIVITY_REL","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/Unit"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"The $\\textit{relative permittivity}$ of a material under given conditions reflects the extent to which\n    it concentrates electrostatic lines of flux. In technical terms, it is the ratio of the amount of electrical energy stored in\n    a material by an applied voltage, relative to that stored in a vacuum. Likewise, it is also the ratio of the capacitance of a\n    capacitor using that material as a dielectric, compared to a similar capacitor that has a vacuum as its dielectric. Relative\n    permittivity is a dimensionless number that is in general complex. The imaginary portion of the permittivity corresponds to a\n    phase shift of the polarization $P$ relative to $E$ and leads to the attenuation of electromagnetic waves passing through the\n    medium. $$\\epsilon_r(w) = \\frac{\\epsilon(w)}{\\epsilon_O}$$, where $\\epsilon_r(w)$ is the complex frequency-dependent\n    absolute permittivity of the material, and $\\epsilon_O$ is the vacuum permittivity.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableSystem":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/CGS"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/conversionMultiplier":[{"@value":"0.000000000008854187817","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/conversionMultiplierSN":[{"@value":"8.854187817E-12","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/dbpediaMatch":[{"@value":"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Relative_static_permittivity","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T0D1"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasQuantityKind":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/DimensionlessRatio"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Relative_permittivity?oldid=489664437","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Relative_static_permittivity?oldid=334224492","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/qkdvDenominator":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E2L-3I0M-1H0T4D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/qkdvNumerator":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E2L-3I0M-1H0T4D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/scalingOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/UNITLESS"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"εᵣ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/ucumCode":[{"@value":"[eps_0]","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/UCUMcs"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/unitForQuantityKind":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/DimensionlessRatio"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/unit"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Relative Permittivity","@language":"en"},{"@value":"Relative Permittivity","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PERM_0DEG_C","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/Unit"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"The rate of water vapor transmission through a specific thickness of a material—i.e., the permeability\n    divided by the thickness.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/conversionMultiplier":[{"@value":"0.0","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/conversionMultiplierSN":[{"@value":"0.0E0","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/deprecated":[{"@value":"true","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/deprecatedInVersion":[{"@value":"3.1.3","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L-1I0M0H0T1D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasQuantityKind":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/VapourPermeance"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/iec61360Code":[{"@value":"0112/2///62720#UAB294","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://cdd.iec.ch/cdd/iec62720/iec62720.nsf/Units/0112-2---62720%23UAB294","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"perm (0 °C)","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"