/conversionMultiplier":[{"@value":"1.0","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/conversionMultiplierSN":[{"@value":"1.0E0","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T0D1"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasQuantityKind":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Count"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/unit"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Sample","@language":"en"},{"@value":"Sample","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NUM"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/SAMPLE-PER-SEC","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/ContextualUnit","http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/Unit"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"The number of discrete samples of some thing per second.","@type":"http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/conversionMultiplier":[{"@value":"1.0","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/conversionMultiplierSN":[{"@value":"1.0E0","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/expression":[{"@value":"$sample-per-sec$","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T-1D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasFactorUnit":[{"@id":"_:n3-4885"},{"@id":"_:n3-4886"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasQuantityKind":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/CountRate"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"sample/s","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/ucumCode":[{"@value":"s-1","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/UCUMcs"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/unitForQuantityKind":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/CountRate"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/unit"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Sample per Second","@language":"en"},{"@value":"Sample per Second","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/SCF","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/Unit"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"The $\\textit{standard cubic foot}$ (scf) is a unit representing the amount of gas (such as natural gas)\n    contained in a volume of one cubic foot at reference temperature and pressure conditions. As such, it is a measure of the\n    actual amount of gas, not the volume of the gas. The reference conditions for standard cubic foot are 60 degrees Fahrenheit\n    and 14.7 pounds per square inch (psi) of pressure.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/conversionMultiplier":[{"@value":"1.1981","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/conversionMultiplierSN":[{"@value":"1.1981E0","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A1E0L0I0M0H0T0D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasQuantityKind":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/AmountOfSubstance"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Standard_cubic_foot","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/scalingOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MOL"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"scf","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/unitForQuantityKind":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/AmountOfSubstance"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/unit"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Standard Cubic Foot","@language":"en"},{"@value":"Standard Cubic Foot","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/SCF-PER-HR","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/Unit"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"The $\\textit{standard cubic foot per hour}$ (scfm) is the molar flow rate of a gas (such as natural gas)\n    contained in a volume of one cubic foot at reference temperature and pressure conditions. As such, it is a measure of the\n    actual amount of gas, not the volume of the gas. The reference conditions for standard cubic foot per minute are 60 degrees\n    Fahrenheit and 14.7 pounds per square inch (psi) of pressure.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/conversionMultiplier":[{"@value":"0.0003328055555555555555555555555555556","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/conversionMultiplierSN":[{"@value":"3.328055555555555555555555555555556E-4","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A1E0L0I0M0H0T-1D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasFactorUnit":[{"@id":"_:n3-4887"},{"@id":"_:n3-4888"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasQuantityKind":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/CurrentOfTheAmountOfSubstance"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/MolarFlowRate"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Standard_cubic_feet_per_minute","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"scf/h","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/unitForQuantityKind":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/CurrentOfTheAmountOfSubstance"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/MolarFlowRate"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/unit"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Standard Cubic Foot per Hour","@language":"en"},{"@value":"Standard Cubic Foot per Hour","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/SCF-PER-MIN","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/Unit"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"The $\\textit{standard cubic foot per minute}$ (scfm) is the molar flow rate of a gas (such as natural\n    gas) contained in a volume of one cubic foot at reference temperature and pressure conditions. As such, it is a measure of the\n    actual amount of gas, not the volume of the gas. The reference conditions for standard cubic foot per minute are 60 degrees\n    Fahrenheit and 14.7 pounds per square inch (psi) of pressure.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/conversionMultiplier":[{"@value":"0.01996833333333333333333333333333334","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/conversionMultiplierSN":[{"@value":"1.996833333333333333333333333333334E-2","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A1E0L0I0M0H0T-1D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasFactorUnit":[{"@id":"_:n3-4889"},{"@id":"_:n3-4890"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasQuantityKind":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/CurrentOfTheAmountOfSubstance"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/MolarFlowRate"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Standard_cubic_feet_per_minute","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"scf/min","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/unitForQuantityKind":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/CurrentOfTheAmountOfSubstance"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/MolarFlowRate"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/unit"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Standard Cubic Foot per Minute","@language":"en"},{"@value":"Standard Cubic Foot per Minute","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/SCM","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/Unit"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"The $\\textit{standard cubic metre}$ (scm) is a unit representing the amount of gas (such as natural gas)\n    contained in a volume of one cubic metre at reference temperature and pressure conditions. As such, it is a measure of the\n    actual amount of gas, not the volume of the gas. The reference conditions for standard cubic metre are 0 degrees Celsius and\n    101.325 kilopascals (kPa) of pressure.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/conversionMultiplier":[{"@value":"42.3105","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/conversionMultiplierSN":[{"@value":"4.23105E1","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/exactMatch":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/SCM_1ATM_0DEG_C"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A1E0L0I0M0H0T0D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasQuantityKind":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/AmountOfSubstance"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"doi:10.1016/B978-1-933762-00-5.50012-8","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"ncim:C2348523","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/scalingOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MOL"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"scm","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/unitForQuantityKind":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/AmountOfSubstance"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/unit"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Standard Cubic Meter","@language":"en-us"},{"@value":"Standard Cubic Metre","@language":"en"},{"@value":"Standard Cubic Metre","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/NCM"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/SCM-PER-HR","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/Unit"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"The $\\textit{standard cubic metre per hour}$ (scmh) is the molar flow rate of a gas (such as natural\n    gas) contained in a volume of one cubic metre at reference temperature and pressure conditions. As such, it is a measure of\n    the actual amount of gas, not the volume of the gas. The reference conditions for standard cubic metre per minute are 0\n    degrees Celsius and 101.325 kilopascals (kPa) of pressure.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/conversionMultiplier":[{"@value":"0.01175291666666666666666666666666667","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/conversionMultiplierSN":[{"@value":"1.175291666666666666666666666666667E-2","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A1E0L0I0M0H0T-1D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasFactorUnit":[{"@id":"_:n3-4891"},{"@id":"_:n3-4892"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasQuantityKind":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/CurrentOfTheAmountOfSubstance"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/MolarFlowRate"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Standard_cubic_feet_per_minute","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"scm/h","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/unitForQuantityKind":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/CurrentOfTheAmountOfSubstance"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/MolarFlowRate"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/unit"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Standard Cubic Meter per Hour","@language":"en-us"},{"@value":"Standard Cubic Metre per Hour","@language":"en"},{"@value":"Standard Cubic Metre per Hour","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/SCM-PER-MIN","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/Unit"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"The $\\textit{standard cubic metre per minute}$ (scmm) is the molar flow rate of a gas (such as natural\n    gas) contained in a volume of one cubic metre at reference temperature and pressure conditions. As such, it is a measure of\n    the actual amount of gas, not the volume of the gas. The reference conditions for standard cubic metre per minute are 0\n    degrees Celsius and 101.325 kilopascals (kPa) of pressure.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/conversionMultiplier":[{"@value":"0.7051750000000000000000000000000001","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/conversionMultiplierSN":[{"@value":"7.051750000000000000000000000000001E-1","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A1E0L0I0M0H0T-1D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasFactorUnit":[{"@id":"_:n3-4893"},{"@id":"_:n3-4894"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasQuantityKind":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/CurrentOfTheAmountOfSubstance"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/MolarFlowRate"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Standard_cubic_feet_per_minute","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"scm/min","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/unitForQuantityKind":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/CurrentOfTheAmountOfSubstance"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/MolarFlowRate"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/unit"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Standard Cubic Meter per Minute","@language":"en-us"},{"@value":"Standard Cubic Metre per Minute","@language":"en"},{"@value":"Standard Cubic Metre per Minute","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/SCM_1ATM_0DEG_C","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/ContextualUnit","http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/Unit"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"The $\\textit{standard cubic metre}$ (scm) is a unit representing the amount of gas (such as natural gas)\n    contained in a volume of one cubic metre at reference temperature and pressure conditions. As such, it is a measure of the\n    actual amount of gas, not the volume of the gas. The reference conditions for standard cubic metre are 0 degrees Celsius and\n    101.325 kilopascals (kPa) of pressure.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableSystem":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/USCS"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/conversionMultiplier":[{"@value":"42.3105","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/conversionMultiplierSN":[{"@value":"4.23105E1","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/exactMatch":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/SCM"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A1E0L0I0M0H0T0D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasQuantityKind":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/AmountOfSubstance"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Standard_cubic_foot","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/scalingOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MOL"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"scm","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/unitForQuantityKind":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/AmountOfSubstance"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/unit"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Standard Cubic Meter","@language":"en-us"},{"@value":"Standard Cubic Metre","@language":"en"},{"@value":"Standard Cubic Metre","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/SCM_1ATM_15DEG_C_ISO","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/ContextualUnit","http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/Unit"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"A $\\textit{standard cubic metre}$ as defined by ISO 91:2017, generally applicable within the oil and gas\n    sectors. The reference conditions for an ISO standard cubic metre are 15 degrees Celsius at 1 standard atmosphere (atm),\n    equivalent to 101.325 kilopascals (kPa) of pressure following ISO 2533:1975.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableSystem":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/SI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/conversionMultiplier":[{"@value":"0.0","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/conversionMultiplierSN":[{"@value":"0.0E0","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/exactMatch":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/SCM_1ATM_15DEG_C_NL"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A1E0L0I0M0H0T0D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasQuantityKind":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/AmountOfSubstance"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"urn:iso:std:iso:2533:ed-1:v1","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"urn:iso:std:iso:91:ed-1:v1","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/scalingOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MOL"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/unitForQuantityKind":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/AmountOfSubstance"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/unit"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Standard Cubic Metre","@language":"en"},{"@value":"Standard Cubic Metre","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/SCM_1ATM_15DEG_C_NL","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/ContextualUnit","http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/Unit"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"The definition of a $\\textit{standard cubic metre}$ conforming to the Dutch Mining Regulations\n    (Mijnbouwregeling) for reporting figures in the Dutch oil and gas industry, and used for liquids except brine (pekel). The\n    reference conditions for a Dutch standard cubic metre are 15 degrees Celsius at 1 standard atmosphere (atm), equivalent to\n    101.325 kilopascals (kPa) of pressure.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableSystem":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/SI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/conversionMultiplier":[{"@value":"0.0","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/conversionMultiplierSN":[{"@value":"0.0E0","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/exactMatch":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/SCM_1ATM_15DEG_C_ISO"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A1E0L0I0M0H0T0D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasQuantityKind":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/AmountOfSubstance"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"http://wetten.overheid.nl/jci1.3:c:BWBR0014468&hoofdstuk=11&paragraaf=11.3&artikel=11.3.1","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"https://open.overheid.nl/Details/fefb9108-c56d-453a-badb-c2ad144da3a1/2","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/scalingOf":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MOL"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"Sm³","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/unitForQuantityKind":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/AmountOfSubstance"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/unit"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Standaard Kubieke Meter","@language":"nl"},{"@value":"Standard Cubic Metre","@language":"en"},{"@value":"Standard Cubic Metre","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}]},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/SEC","@type":["http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/Unit"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"The $Second$ (symbol: $s$) is the base unit of time in the International System of Units (SI) and is also\n    a unit of time in other systems of measurement. Between the years1000 (when al-Biruni used seconds) and 1960 the second was\n    defined as $1/86400$ of a mean solar day (that definition still applies in some astronomical and legal contexts). Between 1960\n    and 1967, it was defined in terms of the period of the Earth's orbit around the Sun in 1900, but it is now defined more\n    precisely in atomic terms. Under the International System of Units (via the International Committee for Weights and Measures,\n    or CIPM), since 1967 the second has been defined as the duration of ${9192631770}$ periods of the radiation corresponding to\n    the transition between the two hyperfine levels of the ground state of the caesium 133 atom.In 1997 CIPM added that the\n    periods would be defined for a caesium atom at rest, and approaching the theoretical temperature of absolute zero, and in\n    1999, it included corrections from ambient radiation.\n  ","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/LatexString"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/applicableSystem":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/CGS"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/CGS-EMU"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/CGS-GAUSS"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/IMPERIAL"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/SI"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/USCS"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/conversionMultiplier":[{"@value":"1.0","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/conversionMultiplierSN":[{"@value":"1.0E0","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/dbpediaMatch":[{"@value":"http://dbpedia.org/resource/Second","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/definedUnitOfSystem":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/sou/USCS"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T1D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasQuantityKind":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ActionTime"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/BurnTime"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/CarrierLifetime"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/HalfLife"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/IgnitionIntervalTime"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/InductanceBasedTimeConstant"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/MeanLifetime"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Period"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/ReactorTimeConstant"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/RelaxationTime"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab