ion":[{"@value":"unit of failure rate","@type":"http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/conversionMultiplier":[{"@value":"0.0","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/conversionMultiplierSN":[{"@value":"0.0E0","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/deprecated":[{"@value":"true","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/deprecatedInVersion":[{"@value":"3.1.0","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasDimensionVector":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/dimensionvector/A0E0L0I0M0H0T-1D0"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/hasQuantityKind":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/Frequency"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/iec61360Code":[{"@value":"0112/2///62720#UAB403","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"https://cdd.iec.ch/cdd/iec62720/iec62720.nsf/Units/0112-2---62720%23UAB403","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/plainTextDescription":[{"@value":"unit of failure rate","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/symbol":[{"@value":"failures/s","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/ucumCode":[{"@value":"s-1{failures}","@type":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/UCUMcs"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/uneceCommonCode":[{"@value":"FIT","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/unit"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"Failures in Time","@language":"en"},{"@value":"Failures in Time","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}]},{"@id":"http://voag.linkedmodel.org/schema/voag#QUDT-DIMENSIONS-VocabCatalogEntry","@type":["http://www.linkedmodel.org/schema/vaem#CatalogEntry"],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/dimensionvector"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"QUDT DIMENSIONS Vocab Catalog Entry","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}]},{"@id":"http://voag.linkedmodel.org/schema/voag#QUDT-QUANTITY-KINDS-VocabCatalogEntry_v1.2","@type":["http://www.linkedmodel.org/schema/vaem#CatalogEntry"],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/quantitykind"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"QUDT Quantity Kinds Vocabulary Catalog Entry v1.2","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}]},{"@id":"http://voag.linkedmodel.org/schema/voag#QUDT-SchemaCatalogEntry","@type":["http://www.linkedmodel.org/schema/vaem#CatalogEntry"],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/schema/qudt"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"QUDT Schema Catalog Entry","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}]},{"@id":"http://voag.linkedmodel.org/schema/voag#QUDT-UNITS-VocabCatalogEntry","@type":["http://www.linkedmodel.org/schema/vaem#CatalogEntry"],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/vocab/unit"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"QUDT Units Vocab Catalog Entry","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}]},{"@id":"http://voag.linkedmodel.org/schema/voag#supersededBy","@type":["http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty"],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/schema/qudt"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"superseded by","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}]},{"@id":"http://www.linkedmodel.org/schema/dtype","http://www.linkedmodel.org/schema/vaem#namespace":[{"@value":"http://www.linkedmodel.org/schema/dtype#","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://www.linkedmodel.org/schema/vaem#namespacePrefix":[{"@value":"dtype","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}]},{"@id":"http://www.linkedmodel.org/schema/dtype#literal","@type":["http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range":[{"@id":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}]},{"@id":"http://www.linkedmodel.org/schema/dtype#value","@type":["http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/EnumeratedValue"},{"@id":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityKind"}]},{"@id":"http://www.linkedmodel.org/schema/vaem#GMD_QUDT-All","@type":["http://www.linkedmodel.org/schema/vaem#GraphMetaData"],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor":[{"@value":"Florian Kleedorfer","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"},{"@value":"Jack Hodges","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"},{"@value":"Steve Ray","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/created":[{"@value":"2025-05-12","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date"}],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator":[{"@value":"Ralph Hodgson","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description":[{"@value":"<p>The QUDT, or \"Quantity, Unit, Dimension and Type\" Collection defines the base classes, properties, restrictions and vocabularies used for modeling physical quantities, units of measure, and their dimensions in various measurement systems. The goal of the QUDT ontology is to provide a unified model of, measurable quantities, units for measuring different kinds of quantities, the numerical values of quantities in different units of measure and the data structures and data types used to store and manipulate these objects in software.</p>\n\n<p>Descriptions are provided in both HTML and LaTeX formats. A quantity is a measure of an observable phenomenon, that, when associated with something, becomes a property of that thing; a particular object, event, or physical system. </p>\n\n<p>A quantity has meaning in the context of a measurement (i.e. the thing measured, the measured value, the accuracy of measurement, etc.) whereas the underlying quantity kind is independent of any particular measurement. Thus, length is a quantity kind while the height of a rocket is a specific quantity of length; its magnitude that may be expressed in meters, feet, inches, etc.  Or, as stated at Wikipedia, in the language of measurement, quantities are quantifiable aspects of the world, such as time, distance, velocity, mass, momentum, energy, and weight, and units are used to describe their measure. Many of these quantities are related to each other by various physical laws, and as a result the units of some of the quantities can be expressed as products (or ratios) of powers of other units (e.g., momentum is mass times velocity and velocity is measured in distance divided by time).</p>","@type":"http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#HTML"}],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified":[{"@value":"2026-09-22T13:10:01Z","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime"}],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/rights":[{"@value":"The QUDT Ontologies are issued under a Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License (CC BY 4.0), available at https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/. Attribution should be made to QUDT.org","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"},{"@value":"\n  This product includes all or a portion of the UCUM table, UCUM codes, and UCUM definitions or is derived from it, subject to a license from Regenstrief Institute, Inc. and The UCUM Organization. Your use of the UCUM table, UCUM codes, UCUM definitions also is subject to this license, a copy of which is available at ​http://unitsofmeasure.org. The current complete UCUM table, UCUM Specification are available for download at ​http://unitsofmeasure.org. The UCUM table and UCUM codes are copyright © 1995-2009, Regenstrief Institute, Inc. and the Unified Codes for Units of Measures (UCUM) Organization. All rights reserved.\n\nTHE UCUM TABLE (IN ALL FORMATS), UCUM DEFINITIONS, AND SPECIFICATION ARE PROVIDED 'AS IS.' ANY EXPRESS OR IMPLIED WARRANTIES ARE DISCLAIMED, INCLUDING, BUT NOT LIMITED TO, THE IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY AND FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.\n  ","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/subject":[{"@value":"QUDT","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://purl.org/dc/terms/title":[{"@value":"QUDT Collection - Version 3.5.2","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/informativeReference":[{"@value":"http://unitsofmeasure.org/trac","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"http://www.bipm.org/en/publications/si-brochure","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"http://www.bipm.org/utils/common/documents/jcgm/JCGM_200_2008.pdf","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"https://books.google.com/books?id=pIlCAAAAIAAJ&dq=dimensional+analysis&hl=en","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"},{"@value":"https://www.nist.gov/physical-measurement-laboratory/special-publication-811","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://www.linkedmodel.org/schema/vaem#graphName":[{"@value":"qudt","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.linkedmodel.org/schema/vaem#graphTitle":[{"@value":"Quantities, Units, Dimensions and Types (QUDT) Collection - Version 3.5.2","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.linkedmodel.org/schema/vaem#hasGraphRole":[{"@id":"http://www.linkedmodel.org/schema/vaem#CollectionGraph"}],"http://www.linkedmodel.org/schema/vaem#hasOwner":[{"@id":"http://www.linkedmodel.org/schema/vaem#QUDT"}],"http://www.linkedmodel.org/schema/vaem#hasSteward":[{"@id":"http://www.linkedmodel.org/schema/vaem#QUDT"}],"http://www.linkedmodel.org/schema/vaem#intent":[{"@value":"Specifies the schema for quantities, units and dimensions. Types are defined in other schemas.","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.linkedmodel.org/schema/vaem#isMetadataFor":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/qudt-all"}],"http://www.linkedmodel.org/schema/vaem#logo":[{"@value":"https://qudt.org/linkedmodels.org/assets/lib/lm/images/logos/qudt_logo-300x110.png","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://www.linkedmodel.org/schema/vaem#namespace":[{"@value":"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://www.linkedmodel.org/schema/vaem#namespacePrefix":[{"@value":"qudt","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.linkedmodel.org/schema/vaem#owner":[{"@value":"qudt.org","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.linkedmodel.org/schema/vaem#turtleFileURL":[{"@value":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/qudt-all","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"}],"http://www.linkedmodel.org/schema/vaem#usesNonImportedResource":[{"@id":"http://purl.org/dc/terms/abstract"},{"@id":"http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor"},{"@id":"http://purl.org/dc/terms/created"},{"@id":"http://purl.org/dc/terms/description"},{"@id":"http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified"},{"@id":"http://purl.org/dc/terms/rights"},{"@id":"http://purl.org/dc/terms/source"},{"@id":"http://purl.org/dc/terms/subject"},{"@id":"http://purl.org/dc/terms/title"},{"@id":"http://voag.linkedmodel.org/schema/voag#QUDT-Attribution"}],"http://www.linkedmodel.org/schema/vaem#withAttributionTo":[{"@id":"http://voag.linkedmodel.org/schema/voag#QUDT-Attribution"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/qudt-all"}],"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label":[{"@value":"QUDT Collection Metadata Version 3.5.2","@type":"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"}],"http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionIRI":[{"@id":"http://qudt.org/3.5.2/qudt-all"}]},{"@id":"http://ww